{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes","id":439267,"title":"Hurt Locker Notes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T20:05:06-07:00","id":439267,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Hurt Locker Notes","content":"Come. Talk Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/into-the-hurt-locker/\" target=\"_blank\">Drafts are right here.</a><br /> <br /> This is where I want to keep the discussion. Keep those rules in mind. In fact, reprinting them here for posterity:<ul><li>First off, notes need to be in one place. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes\">I've set up a forum thread for that</a>. I'll pay attention to that thread.</li> <li>Don't bother commenting on grammar, spelling, and punctuation. These are super raw drafts.</li> <li>Please don't reiterate points. I'm not looking for consensus or &quot;votes&quot;. If someone said, &quot;this issue exists&quot;, don't second it. I don't want to bog down the conversation. If you have a new point or thought, cool. But don't dogpile the conversation, please.</li> <li>Some points don't need context. &quot;This has seven dots, Merits don't go to seven dots&quot; doesn't need context. But, &quot;This is unbalanced&quot; is not really a point that helps anyone. That's subjective. Now, if you played with it, and it created a specific experience at your table, I want to know.</li> <li>Speaking in experiences is good. If you played with something, I want to hear the experiences it created at your table.</li> <li>Please note the positives. This is partly because I want my team exposed to positive notes as well as negative, but also because I want to see what works for you and creates positive experiences. I'm in the business of creating positive experiences.</li> <li>Don't be insulting. Don't insinuate motives from my team. Just address the material; don't try to bring in assumptions and political issues.</li> <li>If you make a &quot;this doesn't work&quot; style note, couple it with what you think <i>would</i> work. That'll help us frame your commentary.</li> <li>Understand that there's some overlap here. A few people did different versions of the same Style, for example. This was by design. I'm not going to &quot;take one but not the other&quot;. But I might strip apart duplicates for alternative maneuvers or similar. I wanted more raw ideas to work with.</li> <li>I will be reorganising and renaming these. Many are a little more specific than I intend. I want to make them more generally useful. If you have thoughts, awesome.</li> <li>At a certain point, I'm going to call an end to notes. At that point, I have to send over my notes to my team, and I can't go back and integrate more ideas.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 03-13-2015, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T21:52:57-07:00","id":439369,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of things I see that I want to talk about in terms of liking, but I want to note first and foremost: Aggressive Driving is my new favorite style merit.<br /> <br /> More coming once I've rea-Well, okay, more likely tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T21:55:28-07:00","id":439374,"title":"","content":"Awesome stuff! Here's my thoughts so far on the normal merits:<br /> Cohesive unit is a little confusing; does it 'refresh' whenever you form a team for a new purpose, or give a new purpose to an existing one? Or do you need to basically lose the merit afterward and buy it again? That said, I really like the idea of having more leader-oriented merits like this.<br /> <br /> The one dot support merit likely shouldn't work on Persistent condition, I'd think.<br /> <br /> At any cost similarly looks like it needs to be made clear how often you can use it. I imagine that's per scene?<br /> <br /> Defender is pretty awesome, and I like how it works both as a defensive, do-gooder type buff and as a fuel for vengeance.<br /> <br /> Know the territory is another really good 'leader' ability, and also seems to be a very good way for a mental oriented character to provide a mundane bonus to combat. I really like that.<br /> <br /> I like the thematics behind Power Object. Reminds me of goetia even if it doesn't force you to indulge on a failure.<br /> <br /> Body as Weapon being a normal merit to do a couple of things that used to be pure FS fare is pretty nice.<br /> Same with Dirty Fighting, though it seems like it could be a dot lower in cost, to me, specifically because it's not a Style.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of the drone style; I assume there's going to be rules for things like drones elsewhere in the book?<br /> <br /> Fair fighter is a nice addition for giving social characters a way to help in combat too (other than calling in allies or retainers).<br /> <br /> Punch Drunk seems... I dunno, I like the idea of it, but it seems a bit too potent, offhand. I imagine playtesting will help find out for sure though.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll glance at the fighting styles a bit later.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:11:57-07:00","id":439383,"title":"","content":"The main thing I want to say as a positive from the first skim is that this inspires a number of characters(my favorite of which is a pansy). Anything that invites stories is a good thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-13-2015, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:14:47-07:00","id":439387,"title":"","content":"I'll definitely have more substantial thoughts later, but I think these are really fantastic.<br /> <br /> Support Network seems to be missing it's mechanics, but it might be late night reading comprehension? Like I see a discussion of the first dot, but not the higher levels and what they offer.<br /> <br /> I also feel like a few of these would be more enticing as 1-2 dot merits, rather than some of them being 3 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:27:27-07:00","id":439414,"title":"","content":"A lot of interesting stuff, very enjoyable. I didn't read everything in exacting detail, but below are my comments on what I've read so far.<br /> <br /> The <b>Dominate Center Line</b> merit: what does &quot;a similarly armed opponent&quot; mean exactly? My assumption is that the defense bonus would apply against any one attacker using a melee weapon or brawl attack, what melee attack would be different enough for it to not apply?<br /> <br /> <b>Grappling</b> Fighting Style: <b>Dynamic Guard</b> merit: <br /> <i>&quot;While prone, your character uses his body to shake and redirect his enemy. Reduce the opponent\u2019s dice pool to grapple by your character\u2019s Dexterity. Unfortunately, your character can\u2019t get up from prone while using this maneuver.&quot;</i><br /> Does this mean reduce your opponents dice pool to establish a grapple with you, or reduce your opponent's dice pool in the opposed grapple test once a grapple is established (what my group loving refers to as Wrestlemania)?<br /> <br /> <b>Grappling</b> Fighting Style: <b>Lock Flow</b> merit: I think this merit is awesome, I love the idea of getting a bonus to grapple by declaring your intended maneuver.<br /> <br /> <b>Kino Mutai</b> Fighting Style: <b>Trained Bite</b> merit: I would suggest stating whether and how this applies to Vampires or other human shaped creatures with lethal bite damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Staff Fighting</b> Style: <b>Thwack Weapon</b> merit: It strikes me that this attack (which, granted, can only disarm) ignores your opponent's defense in favor of forcing a contested roll. I haven't had a chance to try it yet, but I think this might be frustrating for a character who has invested in a strong defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon and Shield Fighting</b> Style: I expected to see a merit that benefits shieldless allies through the use of your shield. That just seems, to me anyway, like a natural area for shield wielding characters to excel. Not a problem, just something I noticed.<br /> <br /> <b>Armed Restraint</b> merit: This merit is awesome and makes me laugh at the possibilities. I assume you would use Weaponry for the grapple attempt using this merit, but that should probably be specified.<br /> <br /> <b>Ground and Pound</b> merit: It's not totally clear to me how this merit works when used in a grapple. Do I have to declare I'm using this maneuver before I attempt the opposed grapple roll? If so does it give me the rote quality on the opposed grapple roll?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3843-drewc","name":"DrewC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:43:58-07:00","id":439424,"title":"","content":"Check out the <b>Mage</b> and <b>Beast</b> hints in the style merits. There's Heroes with Dragonslaying or cultists/followers of Beasts who are Sacrificial Lambs.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm grateful for the things like Falconry, Mounted Combat, and Weapon &amp; Shield for lower tech settings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:03:40-07:00","id":439441,"title":"","content":"Link isn't working?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:11:50-07:00","id":439481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439441#post439441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Link isn't working?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try the link now. <br /> <br /> Also, awesome notes everyone. Keep them coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:52:07-07:00","id":439533,"title":"","content":"I have to say I'm not too keen on Merits that just give bonus dice. I thought we moved away from that with the God Machine rules update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:52:37-07:00","id":439534,"title":"","content":"First off, Bump &amp; Run and J-turn are other words for PIT-manoeuvre and Bootlegger's turn, right? They sound like the same from the descriptions, I just haven't heard those terms used for it before.<br /> <br /> Also; What is the point of One-handed Driving? It's really close to the 3-dot version of Crack Driver, while worse on all counts. It's a nice merit, I just don't see how the same thing merits (ha ha..) two so similar merits.<br /> <br /> And Punch-Drunk... It is kind of unclear. Does it mean that after a character has been brought up to what should give Wound Penalties, all attacks thereafter, no matter how strong, only do 1 level of injury?<br /> <br /> Dirty Fighter is pretty cool, but I don't see the point of the Drawback. Just because someone fights dirty doesn't mean they will betray friends and so on, does it? The drawback implies that it does. And what about in communities where all that matters is the actual result? I don't see hit-men being particularly bothered that someone uses dirty tricks in a fight. Besides, it is awfully punishing. It pushes almost everyone who knows about how the character fights down into Hostile impression. Meaning he has to bribe them to get them to listen to him at all. All in all, I think the drawback is illogical, and not worth the benefits.<br /> <br /> As for Fighting Styles, I think most of them are pretty awesome, but shouldn't Tornado Strike have a penalty of the higher of the number of people within reach, and the highest defence present? Because as it is written, in one-on-one you can freely ignore the opponent's defence, and instead only take a -1 penalty. Or... do you get the penalty AND have to make individual rolls against everyone within reach? If so, it is very unclear on how it works.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Kiriage manoeuvre? Is the bonus on the targeted strikes instead of the penalty for specific targets?<br /> <br /> Other than this? Looks real good!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:03:49-07:00","id":439539,"title":"","content":"I don't think Dirty Fighter needs the drawback, IMO. It's a great merit on its own and the drawback doesn't really feel like it hooks into it in any satisfactory manner. In the same way Choke Hold doesn't need a drawback &quot;people trust you less because you can choke a dude out with your bare hands&quot; I don't really feel like Dirty Fighter needs it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:29:56-07:00","id":439550,"title":"","content":"<br /> Support network is confusing, is professional therapist and support network variant level threes for the merit, and what's level 5? Or at least I presume that is the intent, since if they're separate merits they kind of cover the same territory here.<br /> <br /> Body as weapon seems a little underwhelming to me. For free, one can spend a willpower point to get plus three dice to the roll, which averages to one success, and doesn't suffer a dexterity penalty for a day after, and three precious merit points to make the damage lethal? Wouldn't a roll of quarters do the same thing, for essentially free, no penalty, and no willpower expenditure? A that can be replaced, no not replaced, shown up, by 10 dollars worth of change is kind of a loser.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, love the concept, but the execution needs to be more awesome.<br /> <br /> Dirty Fighter, nice, but the penalty seems a little out of joint with the merit. It's not like, logically, because you hit below the belt people will think you'll just attack them out of the blue. Perhaps a penalty when applying soft leverage (you aren't trustworthy after all), or something else more specific? And if you do keep it as is, is this cumulative with the penalty from face of a thug, err, sorry, air of menace (by the by, I'm totally going to call air of menace face of a thug whatever its name is).<br /> <br /> Fair fighter and dirty fighter probably should have a prerequisite- don't possess the other. Perhaps you thought this was obvious, but it might be worth a little word count nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Punch drunk- interesting, but what about supernaturals? Do werewolves heal twice as slowly here? Do mages or vampires effectively suffer no drawback whatsoever?<br /> <br /> War Cry- What's the point supposed to be? Other than it being used defensively, and well when I think going berserker I don't think of defensive fighting. Maybe if with an exceptional success it could cause targets to run away?<br /> <br /> Manic brutality drawback- wait the berserker takes damage equal to the armor and the weapon takes damage, how does that even work? I'd make it one or the other (if unarmed take damage, if armed weapon takes damage), that makes sense. If that was your intent, well then it needs to be worded a little more clearly.<br /> <br /> Ouch, combine brawling dodge with defensive jab and combination, nasty.<br /> <br /> Is the armor from defensive yell supposed to stack with other types of armor if applicagle? Considering it's nature, i would expect it to.<br /> <br /> I'd write trained bite as plus 2 damage, after all I see no reason why a vampire couldn't train their lethal chompers to do even more damage.<br /> <br /> Tornado Strike- I presume you mean the penalty is minus 1 per target, and not minus 1 to each roll period.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest renaming Parry and Reposte, since the name suggests you should only be able to use it if you parried, ie used a weaponry dodge, but the rules for the technique don't actually require it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-13-2015, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:39:09-07:00","id":439581,"title":"","content":"Defender is the kind of Merit I could see myself building an entire character around, while Cohesive Unit and Know the Territory have such awesome interplay that I <i>need</i> to play someone with both. Living With Death is an interesting way to treat a berserker-esque character beyond just &quot;flip out and murder good.&quot; Mental Scarring is really, really cool. Body as Weapon is a lot of fun. Kiai is my favorite Fighting Style by far, but I do have to ask; why no Style for actual Firearms, just bows and blowguns?<br /> <br /> I hope we can have hints to the minor templates in the book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:58:18-07:00","id":439589,"title":"","content":"I <i>really</i> want to see what Brutal Casting is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:09:23-07:00","id":439595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439589#post439589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>really</i> want to see what Brutal Casting is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Style I wrote for Awakening 2e. You'll see it soon enough. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439589#post439589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope we can have hints to the minor templates in the book!</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll happen sooner than later. I'm waiting on one draft for that section, and I'll be sharing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:10:09-07:00","id":439596,"title":"","content":"There's definitely some great material, but I'll wait a little while for it to digest before offering substantive comments.<br /> <br /> However, teasing the Mage and Beast fighting styles was just plain cruel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:11:19-07:00","id":439598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439596#post439596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's definitely some great material, but I'll wait a little while for it to digest before offering substantive comments.<br /> <br /> However, teasing the Mage and Beast fighting styles was just plain cruel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I totally forgot those notes were in there. I hope they make it into the final drafts with those names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:26:44-07:00","id":439606,"title":"","content":"I may have missed this in the read through, but there is something that I'm wondering about here.<br /> <br /> The tags for Iaijutsu are listed as such:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tags: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Emotion: (Determined), Light Weapons</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, these are the tags for Know the Territory:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tags: Tactical (Military), Tactical (Police), Movement (Agile), Movement (Strong)</span></span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Drone Control is written this way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Style Tags: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tactical (Military) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">or </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Police)</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Is this difference a result of being written by different Authors, or is there some sort of difference in the Style prerequisites?<br /> <br /> There are some very cool ideas in here! I'm loving the fact that Falconry and K-9 are both included and that Mounted Combat has the tactics (police) style (RCMP for the win!). If anything, I'd hope to see even more creature and/or merits that can be used in both modern and historical time periods. Falconry will definitely be getting some use from me as I build my Werewolves of Abu Dhabi Dark Era!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-13-2015, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:24:10-07:00","id":439642,"title":"","content":"After looking through the new merits a bit, I have a bit of a ruling question with regards to Punch Drunk, with regards to Vampires using it in particular. Since Kindred take bashing damage from most lethal sources and stay conscious when their health boxes are filled with bashing damage, and Punch Drunk activates when the user takes more than their last three boxes in some sort of damage, does that mean that the kindred will basically be able to take a bunch of attacks before going down? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:30:37-07:00","id":439645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shomaxt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439642#post439642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking through the new merits a bit, I have a bit of a ruling question with regards to Punch Drunk, with regards to Vampires using it in particular. Since Kindred take bashing damage from most lethal sources and stay conscious when their health boxes are filled with bashing damage, and Punch Drunk activates when the user takes more than their last three boxes in some sort of damage, does that mean that the kindred will basically be able to take a bunch of attacks before going down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Unless the rules get changed, that's how it is. It also allows a human to soak up three bursts of heavy machine gun fire, or tank rounds. It's really... weird in execution.<br /> <br /> I see what they are trying to do, but.. still weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:17:11-07:00","id":439676,"title":"","content":"I noticed there are a couple of maneuvers which involve multiple targets attacking (which is almost like getting back to multiple attacks per turn). Anyway, how do they get resolved? Like for instance, <b>Rain of Arrows</b> (Combat archery 4) is a single dice roll against everybody?<br /> <br /> What about <b>Shihogiri</b> from the Iaijutsu style? Is it a single dice roll against the highest Defense?<br /> <br /> What about <b>Tornado strike</b> from the Staff style? <b>Many blades, One Throw </b>from the alternate Thrown weapon style?<br /> <br /> I second the fact that Weapon and Shield Style should also be used to shield others.<br /> <br /> <br /> ON A MORE GENERAL NOTE:<br /> Some are lackluster, some are good, but the best thing is that <b>it feels like violence</b>, like it was proposed in the outline. It's dirty and messy. Great job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:25:39-07:00","id":439677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shomaxt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439642#post439642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking through the new merits a bit, I have a bit of a ruling question with regards to Punch Drunk, with regards to Vampires using it in particular. Since Kindred take bashing damage from most lethal sources and stay conscious when their health boxes are filled with bashing damage, and Punch Drunk activates when the user takes more than their last three boxes in some sort of damage, does that mean that the kindred will basically be able to take a bunch of attacks before going down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was written with non-supernatural characters in mind, and shouldn't be available to vampires, werewolves etc. I'm following this thread with interest, and any changes that need to be made (such as making character limitations explicit) will be reflected in final drafts.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:44:35-07:00","id":439680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439606#post439606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this difference a result of being written by different Authors, or is there some sort of difference in the Style prerequisites?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Style Tags are new (I invented them in this book!) so there's no format rule for them.<br /> 2) WoD drafts are written in conformity with a specific template and formatting rules. Not all the drafts have been changed into it yet, so chunks may look different. This is at a petty raw stage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:00:11-07:00","id":439703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439645#post439645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Unless the rules get changed, that's how it is. It also allows a human to soak up three bursts of heavy machine gun fire, or tank rounds. It's really... weird in execution.<br /> <br /> I see what they are trying to do, but.. still weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I think it'll end up working for attacks which would normally cause bashing damage. <br /> <br /> As far as Kindred go, I think I might put out a &quot;developer commentary&quot; talking about the other game lines. Ideally, Kindred using mortal fighting Merits will only benefit as a mortal regarding damage types. So if something gives armor against bashing attacks, it should only give it against unarmed attacks, not a sword that does bashing to vampires. But that's a thing I wouldn't mind commentary and more importantly testing notes on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:08:56-07:00","id":439708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439703#post439703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Kindred go, I think I might put out a &quot;developer commentary&quot; talking about the other game lines. Ideally, Kindred using mortal fighting Merits will only benefit as a mortal regarding damage types. So if something gives armor against bashing attacks, it should only give it against unarmed attacks, not a sword that does bashing to vampires. But that's a thing I wouldn't mind commentary and more importantly testing notes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some thing like this going in the book itself would be very useful IMO.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:24:21-07:00","id":439716,"title":"","content":"I'll address some related to my stuff:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrewC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439414#post439414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Grappling</b> Fighting Style: <b>Dynamic Guard</b> merit:<br /> <i>&quot;While prone, your character uses his body to shake and redirect his enemy. Reduce the opponent\u2019s dice pool to grapple by your character\u2019s Dexterity. Unfortunately, your character can\u2019t get up from prone while using this maneuver.&quot;</i><br /> Does this mean reduce your opponents dice pool to establish a grapple with you, or reduce your opponent's dice pool in the opposed grapple test once a grapple is established (what my group loving refers to as Wrestlemania)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrestlemania--I mean, when the grapple is established. This is basically simulating a lot of common open guard defenses in BJJ.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Grappling</b> Fighting Style: <b>Lock Flow</b> merit: I think this merit is awesome, I love the idea of getting a bonus to grapple by declaring your intended maneuver. </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Kino Mutai</b> Fighting Style: <b>Trained Bite</b> merit: I would suggest stating whether and how this applies to Vampires or other human shaped creatures with lethal bite damage. </div> </div> </div>I meant but did not post that the +2B is regardless of the normal damage inflicted--2 bashing tags along. In retrospect though I think a simple +1 damage might be better. With **** Continuous Bite I think tweaking it I would note a +1 damage modifier if the character can already bite for lethal damage, and another +1 of the character has Trained Bite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ground and Pound</b> merit: It's not totally clear to me how this merit works when used in a grapple. Do I have to declare I'm using this maneuver before I attempt the opposed grapple roll? If so does it give me the rote quality on the opposed grapple roll? </div> </div> </div>Should be clarified. It can only be used with the Damage maneuver during a grapple and at the end, the opponent automatically Breaks Free. Otherwise it's a standard Brawl roll. In both cases you end up prone at the end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:42:11-07:00","id":439731,"title":"","content":"I just need to try an Invictii Spina with both the Fair Fighter merit and the Courtoisie fighting style of the Invictus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:42:18-07:00","id":439732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439708#post439708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some thing like this going in the book itself would be very useful IMO.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, we have ten total game lines, if you count the Storytelling System/World of Darkness. If I even give 500 words of notes to each game line, that eats up 5,000 words. This isn't a <b>Vampire</b> book. This isn't a <b>Werewolf</b> book. So I've got to keep it as focused on the core, &quot;mortal&quot; experience as possible. I can put down some notes if I get some time, but it'd take a ton of bandwidth to do justice to ten games. The amount of raw background work one of my team would have to do, then I'd have to do, to deliver that kind of material within the book would be daunting at best, and words wasted on a lot of potential readers at worst. For that 5,000 word assignment, which would normally take a writer about two days, it'd have a research reading requirement of about 3,000 pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 03-13-2015, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:05:36-07:00","id":439776,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more a short sidebar about what Merits do and don't stack with supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:09:52-07:00","id":439779,"title":"","content":"I am currently hosting a military campaign, and I really love these merits. Especially &quot;Cohesive Unit&quot; and &quot;Know the Territory&quot;.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Support Network \u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; Merit is not really clear. Are &quot;Support Network \u2022&quot;, &quot;Professional Therapist \u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; and &quot;Support Group \u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; supposed to be the different levels of this Merit?<br /> <br /> In the &quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; Merit, it is not totally clear whether this ability supplements an attack (i.e. also inflicts damage), or is a diceless attack that only reduces defense. I'd guess it is the second. I also agree with the others that the drawback is not really necessary, especially as it is a 4 dot Merit.<br /> <br /> I was wondering what happens if a character tries to control a drone without the &quot;Drone Control&quot; Style. I'd probably default on a -2 penalty on the Dexterity + Computer roll (if that is stil the dicepool used for controlling drones). But this is probably explained somewhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> Why would anyone take the &quot;One-Handed Driving&quot; Merit, if &quot;Crack Driver \u2022\u2022\u2022&quot; is also available. The latter lets the character perform driving actions as a free action, also making room for performing other actions and in this case without the -2 penalty of the &quot;One-Handed&quot; driving Merit.<br /> <br /> I'll check out the fighting styles later today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:24:50-07:00","id":439787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439776#post439776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking more a short sidebar about what Merits do and don't stack with supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that largely depends on the supernatural power. <br /> A Vampires resistance is different from Werewolves natural armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:27:46-07:00","id":440008,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Two Merits I both like/dislike at the same time:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\">Headbutt and Poison Weapon. They both have the same problem: Cool rules that I'm glad to see spelled out in the game, but are immediately gated behind spending Merit dots to just do a thing. Wanna headbutt somebody? Here's some rules for it! Awesome! That'll just be 2 merit dots' worth of xp to hit someone's head with your head, thank you. I understand from a mechanical-conceptual level that there's a &quot;well here's how you do it without hurting yourself&quot; situation, but...why have it that way? If you want headbutting in the game, just explaining how (with this merit's text) would be great, and enough. If you want a Merit for specializing in skull-to-skull shenanigans, maybe make something where the possessor is Hard-Headed and gets a bonus to the rolls instead.<br /> Wanna coat a weapon in poison? Again, here's how! But you need Int 3, Medicine 2, Science 2, and 4 or 5 merit dots spent. Oh and if you fail the application roll, now it's your problem. Which would be fine, if not for costing 4/5 merit dots, a couple skill/stat prereqs, and in-game whatever costs are deemed by your ST. Making it a general thing (and making acquisition/application easier/more certain) with a Merit would be an approach that resembles &quot;anyone can, but some people do it WELL&quot; more than the D&amp;D 3e feat evoking feel of these Merits as they stand.<br /> <br /> Really cool ideas, though.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/265-cbn","name":"CBN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:57:12-07:00","id":440077,"title":"","content":"So, something that occurred to me while looking at the fighting style deconstruction content (which I think using tags to make flexible prerequisites is really cool) is that I may have flawed understanding of some of the maths.<br /> <br /> I was under the impression that all forms of complex costs were expelled in 2nd ed, thus style merits are effectively a set of one dot merits that must be bought in sequence. If this is the case then the alternative prerequisites system is far more experience cost heavy than the vanilla one.<br /> <br /> Are Style merits supposed to be the last bastion of exponential xp costs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:00:16-07:00","id":440082,"title":"","content":"I always described some of the damage done in a grapple as headbutts and chokes, even if the character does not have these Maneuvers as Merits. My rationale is that the Merits represent a certain level of mastery that affords them the additional benefits described. Otherwise a headbutt is not any more dangerous than a good punch or kick.<br /> <br /> That being said, I can certainly see where you are coming from and have similar feelings. In this case, though, I would simply recommend giving all characters access to these maneuvers for free. Possibly using the rules from <b>Mirrors </b>to custom-build attacks (which I really loved for 1e combat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:40:51-07:00","id":440434,"title":"","content":"These all look great. I'm really excited or this book.<br /> <br /> My only observation so far is that the Torturer Merit might be better as one dot, rather than two, especially when compared to Vice-Ridden in God-Machine, which has a similar but broader application for the same price. Or maybe Torturer could do a little more, like add a Specialty to Intimidation or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:31:35-07:00","id":440472,"title":"","content":"Coming from the position of frequent Storyteller I feel like <b>Know the Territory</b> is very awesome, but would benefit from the clause &quot;and has the appropriate equipment&quot; to the Merit in the same section as having appropriate intelligence. If your analysing a map of a locked down fortress and only have some paper clips and bubblegum to spare among your four friends, it's going to be hard to blow those doors or set those traps.<br /> <br /> Nothing more specific than that is needed. Equipment can be handled through other Merits or Storytelling Scenes, but having a RAW clause to deny use of the Merit in impossible or unlikely situations helps many groups maintain suspension of disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:47:03-07:00","id":440492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=439732#post439732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is, we have ten total game lines, if you count the Storytelling System/World of Darkness. If I even give 500 words of notes to each game line, that eats up 5,000 words. This isn't a <b>Vampire</b> book. This isn't a <b>Werewolf</b> book. So I've got to keep it as focused on the core, &quot;mortal&quot; experience as possible. I can put down some notes if I get some time, but it'd take a ton of bandwidth to do justice to ten games. The amount of raw background work one of my team would have to do, then I'd have to do, to deliver that kind of material within the book would be daunting at best, and words wasted on a lot of potential readers at worst. For that 5,000 word assignment, which would normally take a writer about two days, it'd have a research reading requirement of about 3,000 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As you've pointed out, it's not a supernatural book, perhaps instead of working out the mechanics of how the Merits interact with supernatural benefits just add a sidebar, developer commentary or clause (as have been suggested previous) that's something along the lines of....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>***ONLY HUMAN***</b><br /> <br /> These Merits are intended for use with Mortal characters, but feel free to add them to your other World of Darkness games.<br /> <br /> Treat the Merits as benefiting Mortals, for example if a Merit would grant Armour against Bashing damage, this would only apply to unarmed damage as opposed to any Bashing damage a Vampire receives instead of Lethal damage due to being undead. When in doubt, discuss using these Merits with your Storyteller as the final arbitratior of their applicability and use in other World of Darkness games. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Something along those lines leaves open the interpretation for other groups or Storytellers about how the Merits work in their games and keeps the focus on Mortals for the rules and their intended implication. Everyone else who wants something different can take that guideline and extrapolate from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:52:29-07:00","id":440496,"title":"","content":"A lot of things in these drafts I really like. All of the tactical merits and styles are great. But then there a few things I don't really like.<br /> <br /> I'm not very fond of those few manuevers in some of the styles that use mental or social skills. I'm perfectly fine with the leadership and group coordination merits, because those don't alter results that should be based solely on physical prowess with mental/social ability.<br /> <br /> I'm also not fond of all the &quot;attack multiple opponents in one round&quot; maneuvers, partially because they don't seem distinctive enough from style to style. And I feel like a few merits and high rating maneuvers rely a bit too closely on action movie paradigms. And then the whole style or merit suffers from that, because it makes them clash with the tone I usually associate with the World Of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:52:55-07:00","id":440498,"title":"","content":"<b>Mental Scarring </b>implies past mental scarring and past breaking points. Perhaps add a prerequisite of 'Must Have Lost Integrity due to a Breaking Point' to the Merit? Or something that removes Beat acquisition from resolving mental conditions as your conditioned to push past it rather than be hurt and heal gaining new knowledge and experience in the process. It seems quite the strong Merit otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:58:52-07:00","id":440507,"title":"","content":"For clarification on K-9 and Falconry, do maneuvers stating that the character commands the bonded animal to perform the maneuver use up the character's action for the round as well as the animal's? Or is the command a reflexive action for the handler?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:53:42-07:00","id":440540,"title":"","content":"I have heard of Iaijutsu, but I'm not really familiar with it, so I'm going by what you have submitted as to the &quot;spirit&quot; of the style. It took me a few reads and some thinking to follow everything, so my understanding might be flawed.<br /> <br /> Batto (2) has no limitations on the number of times it can be used, so it seems possible to put the weapon away and draw it again to &quot;restart&quot; the batto. I'm thinking this might go against the intent. I consider each distinct combat sequence a scene.<br /> <br /> Scenario 1 - two separate scenes<br /> Fight the guards at the door leading to the boss. Scene 1<br /> Walk through the door and fight the boss. Scene 2<br /> Scenario 2 - everything is one scene<br /> Boss walks out while you are fighting the guards and joins the fight or you enter while fighting guards and boss joins the fight.<br /> <br /> I think the intent is for batto to be used twice, if desired, in the first scenario, but only once in the second scenario. I could be wrong and it is fine to dodge for a turn so you can start up batto again for a long fight.<br /> <br /> Uke Nagashi (4) is the one I had trouble figuring out, but this is how I understand it.<br /> Spend 1 Willpower and add your weapon's damage rating to your defense.<br /> Then, for a turn, when an opponent attacks their attack is automatically negated and the damage they would have done is reflected back onto them.<br /> The attack negation and reflection can occur multiple times during the turn.<br /> <br /> This creates some issues. A logical issue is as your defense decreases after each attack an opponent's chance of damage is increasing, later attackers have it worse. Stronger opponents will be hurting more than weaker opponents, but the combat system isn't set up to compensate for that, more attack is countered by more defense not more health boxes. Normally, you can forego your defense which I think pushes this maneuver out of balance. You negate all attacks and everyone that tries to attack you gets damage reflected back on them as if you were defenseless, both combined is a bit harsh.<br /> <br /> I understand there is a limitation on how long this can be kept up, but this seems like a combat killer. You would have to assume that everyone is familiar with the style and won't attack when this maneuver is used. For that, you can just remove the damage reflection. The automatic attack negation pretty well covers you with that anyway. At least, if your defense was decreasing then it would make sense for close combat attackers to hit you to set you up for a ranged attack or something. Speaking of which, are we considering grappling moves attacks, at least the ones that don't deal damage? You might address this somewhere else in the book.<br /> <br /> I think addressing some issues would bring this back in line. I can only give possible suggestions since I'm not familiar with this style.<br /> <br /> 1. Don't allow the user to forego defense when they are going to be countering an attack. It would make some sense for people to still attack, if only to reduce your defense.<br /> <br /> 2. Limit the number of times you can negate attacks a turn. This isn't very elegant since the number is going to be subjective.<br /> <br /> 3. Eliminate the damage reflection because, practically speaking, it won't come into play. Simple but doesn't seem to fit the intent.<br /> <br /> If I understand the intent here then I think the first suggestion, possibly in conjunction with the second, would keep everything more or less intact. This maneuver isn't quite game-breaking, but it does kill the fun. You could just as easily say &quot;for 1 willpower nobody can attack you in close combat.&quot; Nothing wrong with deterring an action, but this feels more like eliminating a choice. I'm not down with that.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the length, but I had lots of rules to follow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I liked the concept and flair. I just don't think you got out what you put in.<br /> <br /> Note: I just realized that the counter attack is probably not meant to be automatic, but it doesn't change things for me. Don't hit and receive damage or don't hit and possibly receive damage isn't a huge difference to me. I never considered the damage reflection as a bad thing, just unnecessary in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:04:26-07:00","id":440645,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; vs &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; (from GMC): They both occupy the same design space. The effect for &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; is better, as the opponent loses his whole Defense instead of part of it. But on the other side, the effect is also contested. Is &quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; mostly for people who do not meet the prerequisites for &quot;Cheap Shot&quot;? But even then it is weird that both Merits have different mechanics, while doing the same in character. As it stands now you choose between a strong effect that is contested and next turn, and a weaker effect that isn't contested and this turn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention that &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; doesn't even cost Willpower, so even while &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; has more prerequisites, I still think &quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; is too expensive compared to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 03-13-2015, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:49:39-07:00","id":440755,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of each maneuver being a separate merit and using the style tags to build personalized methods of fighting. For styles that have multiple tags (like Iaijutsu, tags: Emotional (determined), light weapons), would you need merits of the appropriate tags for each or in some combination? For example, say a player wishes to purchase Batto for their character without first purchasing Zanshin. Would they need at least one dot each of Emotional (determined) and light weapons tagged merits such as At Any Cost and Rapidity (Light Weapons 1-dot maneuver), or just one or the other?<br /> <br /> Also I share the concern that these maneuvers effectively cost more as individual merits with prerequisites than initially intended, replicating the exponential experience mode of 1st ed rather than the linear experience of 2nd ed. Perhaps all maneuvers cost 1 experience regardless of dot level, but retain their dots associated with their tags for prerequisite purposes? That seems a touch over complicated, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5326-swift","name":"Swift","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:04:27-07:00","id":440843,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming you know the Style lists under each of the Style Tags is incomplete?<br /> <br /> Am I correct in reading that any style included here completely replaces its &quot;God-Machine Chronicle&quot; version (so if using the 1-3 dot Armored Combat Style, the 1-5 dot version doesn't exist), but those styles from that book not reincluded here should be assumed unchanged (like Light Weapon)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:06:26-07:00","id":440844,"title":"","content":"So with each maneuver being a separate merit in this way, do they have their dot rating as the exp cost then rather than 1xp? Or does meeting the prerequisites count as having spent the prior exp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:06:46-07:00","id":440845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440843#post440843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming you know the Style lists under each of the Style Tags is incomplete?<br /> <br /> Am I correct in reading that any style included here completely replaces its &quot;God-Machine Chronicle&quot; version (so if using the 1-3 dot Armored Combat Style, the 1-5 dot version doesn't exist), but those styles from that book not reincluded here should be assumed unchanged (like Light Weapon)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll be supplementary. The GMC version of Armored Combat will exist; I'll probably strip the one in Hurt Locker thus far, and turn it into individual manoeuvres, or I might change the name up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:21:15-07:00","id":440853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440844#post440844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with each maneuver being a separate merit in this way, do they have their dot rating as the exp cost then rather than 1xp? Or does meeting the prerequisites count as having spent the prior exp?</div> </div> </div> </div>The dot rating should be the cost. <br /> <br /> I should probably note though; when developing, I tend to make things cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:34:11-07:00","id":440865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440853#post440853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The dot rating should be the cost.<br /> <br /> I should probably note though; when developing, I tend to make things cheaper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you would have to buy each one individually. So instead of a fighting style being 5 exp, it would be 15? That sounds terribly regressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:41:48-07:00","id":440872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440865#post440865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you would have to buy each one individually. So instead of a fighting style being 5 exp, it would be 15? That sounds terribly regressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one are you talking about? If I broke up a fighting style, it'd probably be mostly one and two dot Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:52:46-07:00","id":440879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440872#post440872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which one are you talking about? If I broke up a fighting style, it'd probably be mostly one and two dot Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, seems like I don't quite understand the way that the Style tags and this chart works:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merit Dots </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prerequisite Merit Dots (Same Style Tag)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">0</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:13:50-07:00","id":440888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440645#post440645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; vs &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; (from GMC): They both occupy the same design space. The effect for &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; is better, as the opponent loses his whole Defense instead of part of it. But on the other side, the effect is also contested. Is &quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; mostly for people who do not meet the prerequisites for &quot;Cheap Shot&quot;? But even then it is weird that both Merits have different mechanics, while doing the same in character. As it stands now you choose between a strong effect that is contested and next turn, and a weaker effect that isn't contested and this turn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention that &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; doesn't even cost Willpower, so even while &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; has more prerequisites, I still think &quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; is too expensive compared to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind Dirty Fighter applies the Defense reduction to everyone's attacks against the victim. Cheap Shot is good for solo encounters, but if you bring your gang of thugs to back you up, Dirty Fighter is the superior choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:15:02-07:00","id":440890,"title":"","content":"Assuming that the Prerequisite chart is trying to scale to the vanilla fighting style rules, the aforementioned progression skews to merits having an Exponential merit costs (1-3-6-10-15). Buying the 5th dot on that chart requires one to have already spent at least 10 experiences, whereas if style merits are flat cost, the 5th dot would require one to have only spent 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:22:46-07:00","id":440897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440890#post440890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that the Prerequisite chart is trying to scale to the vanilla fighting style rules, the aforementioned progression skews to merits having an Exponential merit costs (1-3-6-10-15). Buying the 5th dot on that chart requires one to have already spent at least 10 experiences, whereas if style merits are flat cost, the 5th dot would require one to have only spent 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is essentially the contention, unless each merit that you meet the prerequisites for only costs 1xp. It is radically different if using that system than the standard (and in fact triples the cost of getting to the 5th dot). This seems rather odd considering the move away from that model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:30:01-07:00","id":440905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440897#post440897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is essentially the contention, unless each merit that you meet the prerequisites for only costs 1xp. It is radically different if using that system than the standard (and in fact triples the cost of getting to the 5th dot). This seems rather odd considering the move away from that model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I see what you mean. As it stands, yes, it means it takes longer to get to those pinnacle levels. But it's not that it inherently costs more; it just means you have to have taken a more diverse path to get there. If you've spent 15 Experiences, it's not that the one Style costs 15, it's that you've built a collection of 15 Merits across various disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:32:43-07:00","id":440907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440905#post440905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. I see what you mean. As it stands, yes, it means it takes longer to get to those pinnacle levels. But it's not that it inherently costs more; it just means you have to have taken a more diverse path to get there. If you've spent 15 Experiences, it's not that the one Style costs 15, it's that you've built a collection of 15 Merits across various disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But if you can't get the 5th dot until you have 10 other dots, and that 5th dot is a 5 dot merit, does that not mean you've spent 15 exp? Or is each maneuver only 1 exp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:06:45-07:00","id":440929,"title":"","content":"I finished reading the fighting merits and I liked the variety. I think Avoidance is my favorite because of the unique concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:12:05-07:00","id":440932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440907#post440907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But if you can't get the 5th dot until you have 10 other dots, and that 5th dot is a 5 dot merit, does that not mean you've spent 15 exp? Or is each maneuver only 1 exp?</div> </div> </div> </div>Style Merits cost 1-5 Experiences, not 1-15. Every dot costs one Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:34:01-07:00","id":440972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440932#post440932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Style Merits cost 1-5 Experiences, not 1-15. Every dot costs one Experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm having an issue with the disconnect of them as individual merits. Going that route just puts them back to 1e territory, and the chart confuses things more to me. So I need to buy 10 dots worth of style merits before I can buy a 5th dot. If I bought all 5 dots of a style, according to that chart and the way that section reads, I would have to buy them as a 1 dot, a 2 dot, a 3 dot, a 4 dot, and a 5 dot merit. I get that each dot costs 1 exp, but if a 5 dot maneuver is a 5 dot merit, it costs 5 exp. And requires you to have bought 10 exp worth of previous merits. Basically costing 15 exp for what would have been 5 exp otherwise.<br /> <br /> Normal route 1-5 = 5 exp.<br /> <br /> By that chart, buying each maneuver individually 1-5 = 15exp (1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5). 5 merits with incrementing ratings. Why would someone ever buy just the 5th dot having enough other dots? Why have 2 different xp systems associated with style merits? I understand one is an alternative, but separating them out its almost always better to go the normal 2e route in this regard.<br /> <br /> I think we're having some disconnect on that somewhere or completely misunderstanding of each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:43:49-07:00","id":440999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440645#post440645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dirty Fighter&quot; vs &quot;Cheap Shot&quot; (from GMC): They both occupy the same design space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, just brainstorming here, how's this for potential replacement effect for Dirty Fighter (ignore costs, prerequisites and drawbacks for now):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Effect:</b> Your character fights rough and uses any underhanded trick to gain advantage. He'll throw sand in his opponent's face, kick below the belt, and beg for surrender to gain the chance to stab his opponent when her guard is down. In combat, the character gains +2 dice to inflict Tilts related to dirty tactics and unfair blows. These include Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, Knocked Down, and Leg Wrack, as well as other Tilts as determined by the Storyteller. Each Tilt can only be applied once per opponent per combat, as she learns to beware the character's tactics.</span></span><br /> <br /> Other options I'm tossing up are 'On a successful attack, spend a Willpower point to apply a Tilt', thereby foregoing the need to roll for the Tilt, but adding a cost.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-14-2015, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:45:26-07:00","id":441000,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, the idea is this: you want, let's say, Combat Archery 5, Trick Shot. But you look and say, &quot;Combat Archery 1-4 is kinda lame; I'd rather spend my Experiences on other stuff,&quot; then you can. The trade-off is that you have to pick up 10 dots' worth of stuff (rather than 4) before you're allowed to do it. So it costs more, but you end up with a character sheet you like better, filled with things you wanted there, rather than detritus you were forced to pick up as prereqs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:36:45-07:00","id":441119,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit sketchy on some of the choices made here but a lot of it's pretty good.<br /> <br /> I feel like I should contribute more than just... This, but I have to say that Mounted Combat feels like it needs rejiggering. Horses provide a lot of benefits; increased mobility is obvious, sure, but also a height advantage that forces your opponents to have to swing above their shoulders to hit you, greatly diminishing their capacity to do you harm. They also provide a lot of shock and awe.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious if Trunk Squeeze and Choke Hold synergize at all. Their benefits are very similar. Can you get a combined Squeeze Choke maneuver?<br /> <br /> Finally, a comment on the Berserker style that feels sort of emblematic of a common issue I have: The War Cry ability reduces an opponent's dice pools that turn but it costs the character an attack. This means that, if someone was playing a Wild Man style lunatic with this style, instead of charging in like a frenzied bear, foaming at the mouth and shouting incoherently, they pause, and yell, and <i>then</i> attack on their next turn after the effect has ended. This feels like a problem. A Berserker's style should reward them for running into the fray head-long without any sense of self-preservation, not rewarding team tactics which, ultimately, is what this maneuver does.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> My proposals on how to fix this would be:<br /> <br /> 1. Mounted Combat should definitely focus on the motion and the charge, but give us something that makes it a true advantage. Fixed Charge doesn't exactly add a tremendous benefit (it could honestly be argued to be adding a disadvantage). Could we replace it with, say, something that allows for a roll to intimidate defenders? Those who fail either turn and run or lose their defense.<br /> <br /> 2. Rearing Beast isn't exactly great. It lets the player risk losing a turn in exchange for a chance to attack with a pool of nine dice. The dice pool isn't bad, but most player characters who are dedicated enough to have four dots in a combat style are probably going to be wielding that anyway. Instead, I recommend creating a Tilt of some sort that's automatically applied to those who try to enter close combat with the cavalier; either they suffer attack penalties or risk being hurt/knocked prone by a thousand pounds of whirling muscle.<br /> <br /> 3. I also recommend adding some sort of benefit for attacking fleeing opponents in here somewhere. Light Cavalry - and cavalry in general after the invention of the gun - had the job of chasing down routed opponents. As a build-off of the aforementioned routing ability that could replace Fixed Charge, perhaps some sort of benefit that'd let a cavalier be extra-effective at stabbing folks in the back?<br /> <br /> 4. For the Berserker, have their War Cry be a part of an all-out attack (encouraging that method of fighting) and make it cause their opponent to hesitate. A crazed maenad charging at her opponent in the woods should utterly surprise them. Perhaps model it off of Cheap Shot, except allow Presence + Intimidation vs. Resolve + Composure; if the opponent fails, they lose their defense as they hesitate at the sight of a naked madwoman with claws bursting from the bushes with murder in her eyes.<br /> <br /> The Fighting Styles in GMC were more than just little tricks. Someone with five dots in the core Martial Arts style starts out relatively simple but, by the end, they're an always-armed nightmare that can beat down people in riot gear. Marksmanship makes precision shooting exceptionally potent for the right character with the right opportunities. I didn't get these same feelings - these feelings of <i>weight</i> - from a lot of the stuff here and I'm sure I could do a more thorough review later if you wanted more commentary, but I'm looking into a possible medieval game soon and Mounted Combat, Archery, Berserks, etc., are all important to me. Spearmen are too, but that style definitely had more of an understanding of making someone trained in the style a very different opponent than one who merely has the weapon to begin with.<br /> <br /> More sensible minds may differ. I'm still greatly looking forward to Hurt Locker. These are just my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:55:16-07:00","id":441129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441119#post441119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More sensible minds may differ. I'm still greatly looking forward to Hurt Locker. These are just my thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, no. All valuable notes. <br /> <br /> Like I said, these are super raw. I haven't edited them yet, and they're in first draft form. This is why I'm putting it out here; I want to make the public part of the process. <br /> <br /> I assure you, many of the things said in this thread are things I'd be thinking, likewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T04:06:07-07:00","id":441182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440999#post440999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, just brainstorming here, how's this for potential replacement effect for Dirty Fighter (ignore costs, prerequisites and drawbacks for now):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Effect:</b> Your character fights rough and uses any underhanded trick to gain advantage. He'll throw sand in his opponent's face, kick below the belt, and beg for surrender to gain the chance to stab his opponent when her guard is down. In combat, the character gains +2 dice to inflict Tilts related to dirty tactics and unfair blows. These include Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, Knocked Down, and Leg Wrack, as well as other Tilts as determined by the Storyteller. Each Tilt can only be applied once per opponent per combat, as she learns to beware the character's tactics.</span></span><br /> <br /> Other options I'm tossing up are 'On a successful attack, spend a Willpower point to apply a Tilt', thereby foregoing the need to roll for the Tilt, but adding a cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of making it easier to inflict Tilts wilt Dirty Fighter, especially as it is a logical consequence of fighting dirty. It is important to remember here that Tilts are normally applied by targeted attacks. So this Merit could give bonusses on those targeted attacks, but that would cause a bit of overlap with other Merits that give those bonusses. Unless you decide that with this Merit targeted attacks are not necessary anymore, which is sort of weird.<br /> <br /> Automatically applying tilts for Willpower is also very nice, as it makes the Merit something more than a dice adder. Especially if it counts as some kind of reflexive secondary attack that only inflicts a Tilt and is always successful (if the primary attack is also successful). This way the character could perform a normal attack (or even a targeted attack to inflict a Tilt), and inflict a (possibly second) Tilt for a Willpower without having to worry about making targeted attacks. This would show some kind of mastery of dirty combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:55:59-07:00","id":441376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441000#post441000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand correctly, the idea is this: you want, let's say, Combat Archery 5, Trick Shot. But you look and say, &quot;Combat Archery 1-4 is kinda lame; I'd rather spend my Experiences on other stuff,&quot; then you can. The trade-off is that you have to pick up 10 dots' worth of stuff (rather than 4) before you're allowed to do it. So it costs more, but you end up with a character sheet you like better, filled with things you wanted there, rather than detritus you were forced to pick up as prereqs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But wouldn't Combat archery 5 still cost 5 exp (the same cost of getting 1-5) in that event? That's what I'm saying here is odd. I understand the RP implications, but it seems to be a rather poor suited way for them to be individual merits when getting the whole style would be just the same as just getting the last dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 03-14-2015, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:05:14-07:00","id":441682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441376#post441376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But wouldn't Combat archery 5 still cost 5 exp (the same cost of getting 1-5) in that event? That's what I'm saying here is odd. I understand the RP implications, but it seems to be a rather poor suited way for them to be individual merits when getting the whole style would be just the same as just getting the last dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way these rules make sense is by saying that style Merits always cost 1 xp no matter the number of dots, but you do take the number of dots into account as prerequisites for further Style Merits. This would mean that Style Merits become it's own thing, with a different XP cost from normal Merits. Doing this would both allow for normal Style progression and normal costs, as the prerequisites for the next Style Merit is always the sum of the previous levels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:10:29-07:00","id":441768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441682#post441682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only way these rules make sense is by saying that style Merits always cost 1 xp no matter the number of dots, but you do take the number of dots into account as prerequisites for further Style Merits. This would mean that Style Merits become it's own thing, with a different XP cost from normal Merits. Doing this would both allow for normal Style progression and normal costs, as the prerequisites for the next Style Merit is always the sum of the previous levels.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what I had thought it might have meant, but that doesn't seem to be the case. Its very confusing and conflicting with the way the new rules work (and totally not worth using such a system when the original is available). I'd like to see some revision in that regard or some major major clarification in that section of the text. If each Maneuver cost 1 exp, but had a rating, and prerequisite combined rating, that would be much closer to the current system and be free of the major exp disparity between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:39:03-07:00","id":441797,"title":"","content":"Very excited with what I've read so far.<br /> <br /> Only thing I don't agree with it the Drawback for Dirty Fighting, as others have pointed out. I just don't see the correlation between fighting dirty and using every advantage to win the fight, and not being able to be trusted by friends and allies. You can be a dirty fighter and still be trusted by your allies. The two are not mutually exclusive. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, great work David!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:29:22-07:00","id":441888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441119#post441119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also curious if Trunk Squeeze and Choke Hold synergize at all. Their benefits are very similar. Can you get a combined Squeeze Choke maneuver?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're different grappling maneuvers (the Merits unlock them) so no--not unless you score an exceptional success or have access to some other special system that lets you apply them both. <br /> <br /> Now the funny thing is that in the real world this represents a body triangle, from which a rear naked choke is the most common submission. However it wouldn't do to automatically combine them. So one suggested tweak might be that you only stop imposing the penalty *after* you attempt a different maneuver. This reflects the real-world application, which generally softens someone up for a different submission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T20:56:07-07:00","id":442141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to second this.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Dude:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The first post of this thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Please don't reiterate points. I'm not looking for consensus or &quot;votes&quot;. <b>If someone said, &quot;this issue exists&quot;, don't second it.</b> I don't want to bog down the conversation. If you have a new point or thought, cool. But don't dogpile the conversation, please.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:02:38-07:00","id":442145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=442141#post442141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Dude:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, redacted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:48:04-07:00","id":442218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=441888#post441888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're different grappling maneuvers (the Merits unlock them) so no--not unless you score an exceptional success or have access to some other special system that lets you apply them both.<br /> <br /> Now the funny thing is that in the real world this represents a body triangle, from which a rear naked choke is the most common submission. However it wouldn't do to automatically combine them. So one suggested tweak might be that you only stop imposing the penalty *after* you attempt a different maneuver. This reflects the real-world application, which generally softens someone up for a different submission.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can stack according to the rules for stacking fighting merits in the excerpt: Stacking fighting merits requires 5 things.<br /> <br /> 2 isn't an issue, ditto 3, 4, or 5.<br /> <br /> So the only issue is 1, and that's solved by the player saying &quot;I wrap my legs around my target and squeeze as I wrap my hands around their throat.&quot; Nothing anatomically impossible about that, is there?<br /> <br /> I'm pondering how defensive yell and iron skin should interact. Using the stacked fighting merit rules, I imagine what we're suppose to do is make defensive yell less applicable, iron skin can already provide u to 2 levels of armor against bashing, so defensive yell would only be applicable against lethal and appropriate aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> But I have two issues with that. One is fairness in the rules, it seems wrong to me, a lower level merit making a 5th level merit less useful.<br /> <br /> And secondly, it seems to me logically those two techniques ought to be able to stack. Iron skin can represent body toughening techniques (skin and bone toughening) or reflexive defensive techniques. Defensive yell is a technique involving the muscles, I could certainly see it not stacking with the second explanation for iron skin, but the first?<br /> <br /> It seems to me someone with toughened skin and bones who knows a muscular defensive technique ought to be tougher than someone who doesn't.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd houserule that defensive yell stacks with other forms of armor, I don't know. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-15-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:52:44-07:00","id":443062,"title":"","content":"So, if I have spent 10 experiences (say, to aquire up to the 4th dot in a style), I can buy several 5-dot maneuvers with the same tag? That would make having a lot of high level maneuvers notably cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1937-treelior","name":"Treelior","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T14:41:01-07:00","id":443125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Treelior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443062#post443062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I have spent 10 experiences (say, to aquire up to the 4th dot in a style), I can buy several 5-dot maneuvers with the same tag? That would make having a lot of high level maneuvers notably cheaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the opposite.<br /> <br /> You realize under the current system 10 experiences buys you 2 full fighting styles? If anything that Makes it MORE expensive to buy those under the same style since they would be 5 dot merits, and would leave you without the other 4 merits you would otherwise get. 2e isn't multiplicative. You simply buy each dot at 1 xp, with the Style chart and buying each individually, it makes things significantly MORE expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T16:16:17-07:00","id":443227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443125#post443125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just the opposite.<br /> <br /> You realize under the current system 10 experiences buys you 2 full fighting styles? If anything that Makes it MORE expensive to buy those under the same style since they would be 5 dot merits, and would leave you without the other 4 merits you would otherwise get. 2e isn't multiplicative. You simply buy each dot at 1 xp, with the Style chart and buying each individually, it makes things significantly MORE expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Readings aside, that's not what this is going to end up like. The actual point costs will not increase; potentially the prerequisites will. I'm sorry if I haven't made this abundantly clear enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:14:29-07:00","id":443455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443227#post443227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Readings aside, that's not what this is going to end up like. The actual point costs will not increase; potentially the prerequisites will. I'm sorry if I haven't made this abundantly clear enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So your saying each maneuver is going to still be 1xp regardless of rating so long as you have the prerequisite ratings worth of maneuvers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:47:18-07:00","id":443522,"title":"","content":"Overall I am really excited for this book. The merits presented thus far are largely excellent; most of them feel useful without overshadowing existing merits. I'm also impressed by the variety and flavor. Avoidance is a great style that could work equally well for pacifists, cowards, or tricksters. Fair Fighter is a delightful incongruity. Animal Ken gets not one but three styles to work with. <br /> <br /> Now to specific questions/concerns. Body as weapon (3) seems a bit underwhelming. For one more dot in Martial Arts I can get the same benefit, along with other techniques, and without any of the drawbacks. Especially if mix and match style progression is going to be a thing I'm hard pressed to think of a situation where I wouldn't take the 4th dot that allows me to always deal lethal without spending willpower or suffering penalties later.<br /> <br /> Speaking of style progression, I'm also having difficulty interpreting that passage. Penta's explanation in post 66 makes the most sense to me but I await further clarification.<br /> <br /> Uke Nagashi (Iaijutsu 4th dot) I'm not sure why this merit increases your defense, given that it negates an incoming attack. Does it only counter one attack per turn? Also, raising defense probably lowers the opponent's successes, and if I understand the merit correctly that in turn lowers your counter damage. I like most of this merit but Armed Defense does this particular idea better. Then again Armed Defense is the most abusable fighting style in core 2e.<br /> Also the fifth dot should probably be a contested roll rather than a resisted one since there's no degree of success.<br /> <br /> Strike and Develop (Spear and Bayonet 3rd dot) This is a 3rd dot merit that effectively doubles your successes for weapons that already deal +1 or +2 lethal. Boxing's 4th dot &quot;roll dex bonus damage&quot; is potentially op if paired with fighting finesse (allowing players to double dip dex) but that requires more set up and investment than this. At minimum this is a bonus +1 lethal, and while the damage over time factor is unique I think a inflicting a penalty might be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Double Strike (Two Weapon Fighting 4th dot) I'm really unclear on how this works. Do you split your pool before defense, or after? What if the opponents have different defense scores? Even assuming both opponents have a modest defense of four and my character is a master with ten dice, splitting my remaining six evenly between them and taking a -2 on each leaves me with... 1 die to attack each opponent. This is in no way a good choice and I would be much better served with another merit. <br /> <br /> Kiriage I'm assuming that the +2 targeted strike is after the -2/-3 for specified targets, instead of replacing those modifiers? That is, it effectively reduces the called shot penalty by two rather than eliminating the penalty *and* providing a bonus. So a called arm strike is a 0 and hand is -1, assuming no further modifiers are in place from other styles. I'm not sure it should apply to hands at all, since attacking the hand is already a very minor additional risk for a much higher chance of inflicting arm wrack, so much so that it's only really worth trying for the arms if hands would drop you all the way to chance die.<br /> <br /> Similarly, is Boot Party taking into account the usual +2 to attack a prone opponent (who doesn't have Rolling or Ground Fighting)? I would be interested to combine it with ground and pound for a high risk/high reward move. Take a penalty to your attack and go prone for the chance to inflict massive damage? I'd try it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T19:02:36-07:00","id":443537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443455#post443455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So your saying each maneuver is going to still be 1xp regardless of rating so long as you have the prerequisite ratings worth of maneuvers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fairly certain this will be the case. I don't intend on making Merits cost differently depending on the order in which you buy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T01:45:08-07:00","id":443915,"title":"","content":"<b>Air of Menace:</b> It's a merit that makes a statement about a character. I like merits that makes statements about characters. However, NPCs/Mooks don't have willpower to spend, which means that as long as the character with this merit doesn't throw the first punch, they have a /lot/ of leeway in what they can get away with.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesive Unit:</b> This is a grab-bag of ideas that feels really rough. The pool mechanic is a smidge &quot;eh&quot; in the sense that it's another thing to keep track of. I think the intent, judging from the drawback, is that a group can only benefit from one leader with this merit. That isn't explicit enough. &quot;Actions to help the team&quot; is about as vague as you can get. Drawing on a pool of dice, etc etc are all mechanics and phrasing that are not commonly found in the Storyteller System. Id recommend something more familiar.<br /> <br /> <b>Support Network (first time):</b> I like this conceptually. It has no actual mechanics, though. I'd also almost want it to be cheaper tied to other social merits... Hrm. Maybe, something to bat around.<br /> <br /> <b>Support Network (one dot version):</b> This is listed twice for some reason. &quot;One negative condition&quot; is really vague and will be abused horribly. Do you get a beat for resolving conditions this way?<br /> <br /> <b>Professional Therapist:</b> Feels boring, somehow. Also between this and Meditative Mind, breaking points become pretty trivial pretty quickly. I mean that's also five merit dots so...?<br /> <br /> <b>Support Group:</b> Don't use the phrase &quot;mind rape.&quot; I don't mind it personally but I've gotten in to several hour long discussions with people who are quite passionate about that phrase not being used. Strangely less boring in my mind than Professional Therapist, largely because it represents a certain amount of personal development on the part of the character. My gut says to limit it to 1/story and talk about something that made you lose integrity, to prevent it from becoming routine and boring.<br /> <br /> <b>Torturer:</b> Sure.<br /> <br /> <b>At Any Cost:</b> Complicated and hard to follow. It isn't when you stop to think about it, but you also have to stop to think about it. With two variables (Resolve and Composure) its actual value will vary widely. I also feel like there's going to be some tilt somewhere that's just plain silly when combined with this but... eh.<br /> <br /> <b>Defender:</b> The shounen anime merit! I like the concept. Cost may need to be adjusted slightly. I'd throw in rules for refilling this extra pool (possibly by having a touching or meaningful scene with someone who is your friends / family). More stringent criteria than &quot;friends or family&quot; may be a good idea too, not sure.<br /> <br /> <b>Dominating the Center Line:</b> Epic name for a meh effect. Wording is off, needs to clarify that it triggers on the user's miss and what &quot;similarly armed&quot; means. Or just give it a simpler mechanic.<br /> <br /> <b>Know the Territory:</b> I do not like effects with two variables in them (Wits and Composure) in this case. It looks small, but it can add up. Something in my gut is flagging this merit in general though. The trap option definately needs looking at.<br /> <br /> <b>Living With Death:</b> This is going to stack horribly with other things that affect All Out Attacks. The one Garou fighting style is the first thing that comes to mind (use Totem benefit to pick this up ignoring the prerequisits). I'm sure there's other stuff, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Scarring:</b> &quot;Mental Conditions&quot; is not a game term. The drawback makes for a lot of book-keeping. Like the concept.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Object:</b> I really like the concept. I'd almost say have this trade effects with Professional Therapist.<br /> <br /> <b>Master of the Mask:</b> I feel like this is just Striking Looks with a fancier name.<br /> <br /> <b>Aggressive Driving:</b> ngl, never really look at driving rules, nor do my players.<br /> <br /> <b>Body As Weapon: </b>Feels weak, honestly.<br /> <br /> Drone Control Style: Feels like something yo need just to use drones ata ll? Hard to look at this merit in a vacuum and understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:21:15-07:00","id":443934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443915#post443915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Support Group:</b> Don't use the phrase &quot;mind rape.&quot; I don't mind it personally but I've gotten in to several hour long discussions with people who are quite passionate about that phrase not being used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ick. Didn't notice that in my first skim. It won't make it to later drafts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:26:58-07:00","id":444711,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly interested in the Combat Archery style merit as I have a Hunter/Geist character who likes to bow-stake vampires. The version in the draft here is even better than the homebrew one I made based on the videos of Lars Andersen. One thought though: Should dot 3, Parthian Shot, work against any melee attack rather than being exclusive to grappling? Also, is the dice pool there right? The rest of the Merit uses Strength + Athletics rather than Dex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T14:26:21-07:00","id":444890,"title":"","content":"<b>Armored Combat</b><br /> O - The &quot;wear for a chapter&quot; thing feels like tedium that eats wordcount without much benefit.<br /> OO - Feels weakish. Maybe up it to a -2 penalty?<br /> OOO - Wording is clunky, but it's good.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> I find it interesting that this is a style you take to increase offense, not defense. 3 EXP for +2L damage to your brawl and weapon attacks is nice. This isn't a bad thing, but the name and implications of a combat style centered around armor implies that you take it to be tankier.<br /> <br /> <b>Avoidance</b><br /> O - I love this. For one dot you can make a non-combat character that won't easily get murdered in combat, opening up more concepts in more games.<br /> OO - Eh. Meh? This feels like a sucker punch to your allies. I'd put the choice in the defending player's hands, not the merit-holder's. I mean it technically is, but not in a healthy way &quot;Well I'm not your ally!&quot;<br /> OOO - Hrm... Like the concept.<br /> OOOO - It's definitely a power that should be here. Feels underwhelming for a four-dot maneuver, though.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> I love this concept and definitely want to see it in play. It's something I feel the game needs. The later dots could use some work, in my opinion. If you want to take this style from &quot;really good&quot; to &quot;great&quot; then you need to give someone with avoidance tactical decisions during combat without breaking theme. A tall order, I know.<br /> <br /> <b>Berserker Style</b><br /> O - Cool and thematic.<br /> OO - This is pretty meh.<br /> OOO - This is going to be a pain to keep track of. Really it's use is to make Brass Knuckles and Knives with 3L damage, practically speaking.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> Feels a bit all over the place. I'd like a tighter mechanical thematic. It doesn't feel very berserker-rage-y, if that makes sense. If Warcry was buffed up, maybe moved to dot 3 (affects all opponents, maybe impacts Defense and/or Initiative) it'd be cool.<br /> <br /> <b>Bowmanship</b><br /> O - Nice basic ability. You should so make it +(Merit Dots) instead of +2.<br /> OO - Wait, what? This is referencing what I assume are basic mechanics I'm unfamiliar with. Bows have variable damage now?<br /> OOO - Feels complicated for what it does. I'd just apply Shaken against unaware opponents.<br /> OOOO - Neat. I like it.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> Why the heck does this use firearms when bows normally use Athletics? Or am I wrong there? Otherwise the style is pretty cool and bow users should love it!<br /> <br /> <b>Boxing</b><br /> O - Solid.<br /> OO - I like it, and it creates a clear picture in my head.<br /> OOO - I would just grant brawl attacks the Stun weapon quality and make this the four-dot, personally. That said, it's pretty nice. Is a strike against the head -3 total (-2 then -1) or -2 total?<br /> OOOO - I don't like added dice rolls, personally. This also feels like something that should cost willpower or some such. I'd almost say 8-again is a good mechanic to represent combinations.<br /> OOOOO - This is obscenely overpowered, especially when stacked with other things that add to brawl damage. Armored Combat 3, Boxing 4, Martial Arts 5, Street Fighting 4, etc etc.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> A really solid style with a strong thematic. Needs some tweaks but is definitely on the right track.<br /> <br /> <b>Chain Weapons</b><br /> O - Hrm. I like this. I don't like it as a one-dot power, but I do like it. Feels like too much of a change in the fighting dynamic for one exp. Maybe as a capstone power it's great. This is going to stack in horrible ways with Vigor.<br /> OO - I really like this, and would make it the one-dot power. It feels foundational. I'd make it a flat bonus to grapple rolls if anything, otherwise you'll have magic chains with a +10 bonus.<br /> OOO - Hah, this is pretty fun. <br /> <i>Overall:</i> This style could benefit from going to 4 or 5 dots and a bunch of polish, but it has some cool thematics going on.<br /> <br /> <b>ALTERNATE Chain Weapons</b><br /> O - I like the thematic, but there's a little too much going on and it's a huge wordcount sink. I know it's rough, but. &quot;Targets that attempt to attack you in melee take 1L damage unless they take a -2 penalty to their attack roll&quot; is fine.<br /> OO - Feels boring and speedbump-y. If it had something that built off of it later, it might be cool.<br /> OOO - This is hugely overpowered with allies. An aside, I think light weapon style has something like this, and you can use light weapon style with chains.<br /> OOOO - So... you get a +1, maybe +2 bonus to called shots? Meh.<br /> OOOOO - Chains are melee weapons. There is no &quot;ranged grapple&quot; possible. This is just weird and trying too hard to be epic.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> Not a fan of this aternative version. I could see playing with the ranged attack and aiming mechanic a bit more.<br /> <br /> <b>Combat Archery</b><br /> O - References mechanics I don't have. If bows effectively take a turn to reload in between shots then this merit is mandatory to make them really viable. That's not necessarily a bad thing, and one could argue it's an EXP towards fidelity, but it is something to be aware of when making mutually exclusive styles.<br /> OO - Meh, I'd just negate the penalties all the time.<br /> OOO - This can potentially allow two attacks per turn, which is generally considered bad juju.<br /> OOOO - I like this one. It's cinematic and uses existing rules and etc. Very nice.<br /> OOOOO - This is horrendously overpowered. It allows you to move a great distance (or do other things) to kite opponents /and/ it negates defense. I think the core concept is usable--maybe even worth a style unto itself--but it needs work.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> This one is really rough and I look forward to seeing the next draft. I'm really not sure why this one uses athletics while the other one uses firearms? If you want to put in dice-swapping mechanics I'd make it the one-dot or two-dot power.<br /> <br /> <b>Falconry</b><br /> O - I feel like any small animal you'll actually be concerned about will be supernatural in nature and probably not subject to shaken. Neat idea, but needs different mechanics.<br /> OO - Does the bird do this separately and in addition to your action, or do you sacrifice your action for the bird?<br /> OOO - If you use a falcon's traits for this, then it will always be a chance die.<br /> OOOO - I don't actually understand what this does or how it's suppossed to work.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> I think the animal styles need to be thought out more, and they should work without multiplying the user's actions if at all possible.<br /> <br /> <b>Grappling</b><br /> O - Pretty sure you can already inflict the knocked down tilt with a grapple?<br /> OO - I would just make this a Move and incompatible with the Damage Move. The way it's written, this can be used outside a grapple (-2 attack roll) and you can't get your extra move on an exceptional success.<br /> OOO - I like it! Makes that not-frequently-used maneuver much more interesting.<br /> OOOO - (Dynamic Guard). Weirdly named, but okay for the mechanic side of things. Kinda oddly worded since it isn't really a maneuver?<br /> OOOO - (Lock Flow). Sure. I'd make it apply to Restraining too.<br /> OOOOO - (Tap or Snap). I like it a lot!<br /> OOOOO - (Positional Dominance). This is also pretty great. I fear it /might/ be overpowered, but I'm not sure?<br /> <i>Overall:</i> I really like the work done here. Sure it needs a bit of polish, but it's pretty close.<br /> <br /> <b>Iaijutsu</b><br /> O - This is a pretty huge benefit that isn't really supported by the fluff in an way. You just randomly get a bonus to avoid surprise because you're holding a sword?.Some dissonance there.<br /> OO - I would just make it ignore the penalty in general. Why put the turn tracker in? I'd also make this the one-dot and make it lower the penalty by your dots in this merit (max +0).<br /> OOO - This feels like a four-dot or five-dot maneuver and it needs to sacrifice defense or something. Otherwise it's really cool.<br /> OOOO - This does too much. I'd split it up into two different maneuvers. One for the +Defense, one for the counter-attack. The counter attack is probably too powerful.<br /> OOOOO - This is pretty overpowered.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> Nix the five-dot, swap 2 and 1, shift 3 and 4 both up and find a new 3-dot. This is a really solid style for the most part, but it needs a lot of fine-tuning.<br /> <br /> <b>K-9 Style</b><br /> Effect: Wait so all that falconry stuff requires animal ken rolls?<br /> O - I feel like this isn't really a maneuver so much as a stand-alone merit.<br /> OO - Sure<br /> OOO - I like this one.<br /> OOOO - I like this one too.<br /> <i>Overall:</i> Has all my comments with regards to using animals in fights, but! I like this style a lot more. I could see a polished up version of this making playing with a police dog fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:31:45-07:00","id":445069,"title":"","content":"Combat Archery is a bit too powerful for my liking. Well, except the first dot, which I would keep around as a merit. But over the course of the style, bows start to become better than guns, capable of doing high damage (going as far as burst fire), without the noise and also ignoring defense. It even gets rid of the disadvantage of a target trying to close the distance. If this was a supplement for over the top action, it would be great. But it feels a little too power fantasy to tap into the more horrorfying nature of real violence. It also goes back to athletics for the roll, which I am not a fan of. In GMC, with athletics adding to defense, archers get even more benefit from the stat they use for combat, whereas other fighters have to invest in a merit (which is also only useful when using the skill). I suppose the same is true of thrown weapon fighters, but thrown weapons aren't capable of causing as much harm, generally. In several games I have played and ran, archery running with athletics always came across as overpowered. <br /> <br /> The other archery style is nice. Useful, but without being too much. The Out of Nowhere part is incredibly thematic. As I said before though, the first level of Combat Archery would be a good merit.<br /> <br /> I am absolutely loving some of the more niche styles, like falconry. It really opens up some interesting character concepts, which is always a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5038,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","user":"Oran Solus","date":". 03-16-2015, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","name":"Oran Solus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T16:49:01-07:00","id":445082,"title":"","content":"<b>Know the territory</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Set a Trap for your enemy, This trap will deal 1 Lethal damage for each success you dedicate to this ability. This prevents the enemy from escaping.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>my initial thought is, so vampire's take lethal from very few things... I feel like how the &quot;trap&quot; operates could allow this to be adapted to supernatural entities, instead of specifying &quot;1 lethal&quot;. Presuming this means physical trap and not ambush (can that also be clarified?) characters are allowed to specify if it's anything other than say a steel trap. A silver trap does 1 agg to Werewolves but 1 bashing to vampires (per success). Maybe it's gasoline poured around the area, agg to vamps, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:59:40-07:00","id":445175,"title":"","content":"<b>Avoidance</b><br /> <br /> I had a player that played like this, the problem is that if I design an encounter for 4 players and only 3 are actually participating... (she decided it was a good time to pull out her laptop (as her character) during a werewolf vs true fae. This is even worse when you take 2 players and drop it to 1, focused fire problem, I also told her that I'd make her roll for Integrity loss if she got someone killed by not participating (maybe that was not cool but, if people are fighting for their lives and you're sitting it out, guilt for inaction when someone gets hurt)<br /> <br /> <b>Insignificance</b><br /> Perhaps the first dot could do something like &quot;distracting&quot; all non allied attackers take a -1 penalty to attack because they are paying attention to this character seeing what she'll do.<br /> <br /> As this is if your player isn't participating and the enemy isn't seeking them specifically why would this be necessary? they'd deal with the true threats first...<br /> <br /> <b>Coattails</b><br /> Maybe add the defender gains a bonus to attack +1 (or more?) as long as he's defending the avoider.<br /> <br /> <b>Whack-a-mole</b><br /> actually this one is good, maybe more of them could be like this (heck maybe this should be dot 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Play dead</b><br /> Opponents must make the check and it is an &quot;Instant&quot; action<br /> <br /> <br /> other thoughts, maybe they could all be like whack-a-mole and match the description more. Bonuses to dodge. there could be a dot that the attacker actually has reflected damage. Maybe another causes the attacker to have a dramatic failure. I like the idea that avoidance would allow a player to actually take out an enemy without attacking. This would allow them to be useful to their teammates while avoiding the conflict (I'm thinking slapstick comedy movie fight, enemy throws punch they duck, enemy knocks out his own teammate).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 03-16-2015, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T19:28:46-07:00","id":445225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=443455#post443455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So your saying each maneuver is going to still be 1xp regardless of rating so long as you have the prerequisite ratings worth of maneuvers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You count each maneuver according to dots, so if you can figure out a path, you could buy a 1-dot, 2-dot, 3-dot, and 4-dot maneuver with the same tag spending 4 experience to do so. You would have to meet prerequisites so it could easily require more experience. You could also spend 10 experience on 1-dot maneuvers with the same tag to prepare you for a 5-dot instead. This means you could spend 5 experience to get a 5-dot maneuver or up to 11 experience, not including other prerequisites.<br /> <br /> Note: last sentence is the sum of experience spent on the last maneuver and all maneuvers required to meet style prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-16-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T19:32:59-07:00","id":445228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oran Solus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445069#post445069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat Archery is a bit too powerful for my liking. Well, except the first dot, which I would keep around as a merit. But over the course of the style, bows start to become better than guns, capable of doing high damage (going as far as burst fire), without the noise and also ignoring defense. It even gets rid of the disadvantage of a target trying to close the distance. If this was a supplement for over the top action, it would be great. But it feels a little too power fantasy to tap into the more horrorfying nature of real violence. It also goes back to athletics for the roll, which I am not a fan of. In GMC, with athletics adding to defense, archers get even more benefit from the stat they use for combat, whereas other fighters have to invest in a merit (which is also only useful when using the skill). I suppose the same is true of thrown weapon fighters, but thrown weapons aren't capable of causing as much harm, generally. In several games I have played and ran, archery running with athletics always came across as overpowered.<br /> <br /> The other archery style is nice. Useful, but without being too much. The Out of Nowhere part is incredibly thematic. As I said before though, the first level of Combat Archery would be a good merit.<br /> <br /> I am absolutely loving some of the more niche styles, like falconry. It really opens up some interesting character concepts, which is always a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat Archery is a legitimate reflection of how combat archery works, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T20:42:44-07:00","id":445290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445228#post445228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Combat Archery is a legitimate reflection of how combat archery works, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doing parkour manouvres across walls whilst taking a shot? Loosing three accurate arrows in the space of a few seconds? We have very different experiences of archery. Even if it was like that, in game terms it really upsets the balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","name":"Oran Solus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:08:14-07:00","id":445304,"title":"","content":"@Oran Solus<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:16:42-07:00","id":445309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445304#post445304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Oran Solus<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I knew one of those videos would be coming. :]<br /> <br /> It looks very cool, no doubt, but it just isn't practical. The groupings on a lot of his shots are pretty awful. Keep an eye out for archery forums, much more seasoned archers than I often discuss these videos. The general consensus is that it is a nice skill, but not really practical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","name":"Oran Solus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:45:18-07:00","id":445345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inkpenavenger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445304#post445304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Oran Solus<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BEG-ly9tQGk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Those shots are staged, I doubt a Vampire would let you do fifteen takes.<br /> <br /> It's also not very good parkour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T01:22:36-07:00","id":445465,"title":"","content":"I think it was David Hill who posted a pretty well reasoned countervideo on his G+ feed, which also reflected the google scholar research I did.<br /> Basically, most of the techniques are legit, in that they have been used in different combinations by cultures for war. But they have never been &quot;forgotten&quot; forms of archery, he did not rediscover them, and they are not the be-all-end-all form of archery. The techniques used have some significant drawbacks, which would also have to be modelled.<br /> The cultures that most likely used a close approximation to the hodgepodge of techniques shown in the video in war are the Saracens/Persians, mostly for horse based archery focused on filling the air with as many arrows as possible using bows with a drawstrength of ~50 pounds.<br /> The Romans <i>mercilessly</i> mocked the Persian's style of archery, because it sucks against anyone wearing heavy armor. Even with the high accuracy ancient archery manuals we have for the Saracens give as an average and used at short distances thanks to the horses' high mobility, these weren't enough to make up for the lack of piercing power against the Romans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-17-2015, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T01:48:51-07:00","id":445479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=442218#post442218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can stack according to the rules for stacking fighting merits in the excerpt: Stacking fighting merits requires 5 things.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't because each Merit unlocks a new grappling maneuver in addition to the default list, so these are controlled by the grappling rules, which state 1 maneuver unless you score an exceptional success. This may be worth clarifying through.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:35:46-07:00","id":445728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445465#post445465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was David Hill who posted a pretty well reasoned countervideo on his G+ feed, which also reflected the google scholar research I did.<br /> Basically, most of the techniques are legit, in that they have been used in different combinations by cultures for war. But they have never been &quot;forgotten&quot; forms of archery, he did not rediscover them, and they are not the be-all-end-all form of archery. The techniques used have some significant drawbacks, which would also have to be modelled.<br /> The cultures that most likely used a close approximation to the hodgepodge of techniques shown in the video in war are the Saracens/Persians, mostly for horse based archery focused on filling the air with as many arrows as possible using bows with a drawstrength of ~50 pounds.<br /> The Romans <i>mercilessly</i> mocked the Persian's style of archery, because it sucks against anyone wearing heavy armor. Even with the high accuracy ancient archery manuals we have for the Saracens give as an average and used at short distances thanks to the horses' high mobility, these weren't enough to make up for the lack of piercing power against the Romans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was the one that posted it. And basically what you said there. <br /> <br /> That said, it could be practical in an urban fantasy/horror setting. It's not impossible/superhuman in the real world; just nothing anyone would care to learn unless their schtick is making Youtube videos. Now, if you're being assailed by monsters who stop when you put a rowan shaft in their chest, that becomes a much more viable prospect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:03:55-07:00","id":446106,"title":"","content":"With such low draw strength and the inaccuracy of the shots, I just don't see it working. And learning trick shots for youtube isn't the same as using it in a real violence situation. You don't get multiple takes and get to practice the exact same shot multiple times. Camera editing doesn't work in real life.<br /> <br /> I can do some really cool martial arts tricks, that look amazing on camera. Useless in a fight though.<br /> <br /> If it really has to stay, I would at least recommended turning it down a little. Bows have already been plenty powerful in the games I have run. <br /> <br /> I much prefer the other archery merit. It plays into the 'realism' of violence, and complements archery without overselling it. I think that's all I can really say on the subject. I don't want to take the whole thread up when there is plenty of other content where feedback is probably appreciated. I'll have another read and see what else I can say that could be in any way helpful. By and large, I'm really liking it so far. Violence is truly terrorfying, and the merits are pretty good at reinforcing that theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5038,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","user":"Oran Solus","date":". 03-17-2015, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5038-oran-solus","name":"Oran Solus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:56:34-07:00","id":446576,"title":"","content":"Any planned Merits or Styles dealing with generic Supernatural grab bag tricks and advantages? Or is that going to be part of other sections? Nothing specific, it's just what good is stuff that'll work on a human against monsters that have inhuman qualities and/or abilities that subverts the &quot;why&quot; behind what works?<br /> <br /> Knives? Undead can just use their hand to catch the blade inside said hand and lock their still working hand around yours, monsters with exceptionally tough skin will straight up break the cheap and flimsy (Chinese wall pieces,box cutters, etc.) stuff.<br /> <br /> Grappling? Obviously you wouldn't grapple someone on fire or obvious hazards but the non-obvious ones like not actually having bones, or worse super strength where it could straight up twist your arm around like a chicken before crushing your throat with a quick clench of it's hand.<br /> <br /> Ranged? Supernatural speed clears the distance at a much more significant distance then at the same speed as a mundane human would (which if I remember correctly is within 20-21 feet, or 7 yards) then there is dealing with Supernatural ranged attacks if you don't have ranged capabilities onhand yourself.<br /> <br /> Defenses against Indirect Attacks (from elsewhere, the monster is invisible, etc.)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-17-2015, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T15:56:37-07:00","id":446631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446576#post446576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any planned Merits or Styles dealing with generic Supernatural grab bag tricks and advantages? Or is that going to be part of other sections? Nothing specific, it's just what good is stuff that'll work on a human against monsters that have inhuman qualities and/or abilities that subverts the &quot;why&quot; behind what works?<br /> <br /> Knives? Undead can just use their hand to catch the blade inside said hand and lock their still working hand around yours, monsters with exceptionally tough skin will straight up break the cheap and flimsy (Chinese wall pieces,box cutters, etc.) stuff.<br /> <br /> Grappling? Obviously you wouldn't grapple someone on fire or obvious hazards but the non-obvious ones like not actually having bones, or worse super strength where it could straight up twist your arm around like a chicken before crushing your throat with a quick clench of it's hand.<br /> <br /> Ranged? Supernatural speed clears the distance at a much more significant distance then at the same speed as a mundane human would (which if I remember correctly is within 20-21 feet, or 7 yards) then there is dealing with Supernatural ranged attacks if you don't have ranged capabilities onhand yourself.<br /> <br /> Defenses against Indirect Attacks (from elsewhere, the monster is invisible, etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not doing anything specifically for supplement and other game line characters. However, I will be adding a few &quot;minor template&quot; style character types, and some general supernatural Merits. But, blue book stuff, not for the other lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:06:40-07:00","id":446656,"title":"","content":"I don't mean anything line specific, just generic Supernatural stuff in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:50:48-07:00","id":446705,"title":"","content":"Okay, first off, I like what I see so far! The Thrown Weapon Styles are awesome, and something I plan to playtest. The Falconry, K-9, and Mounted Combat styles are also awesome. The Falconry Style, especially, is a personal favorite of mine because it's just so unique. When was the last time you've seen falconry handled in a tabletop game?<br /> <br /> That said, talking with a couple fellow players did brings up a few concerns. Bowmanship uses Dexterity+Firearms in it's attacks, while Combat Archery uses Strength+Athletics. One person brought up how (to our knowledge) archery rules in general haven't been addressed, and hoped we'd get a firm dicepool for it in Hurt Locker. This was coming off a huge debate about thrown weapons and if the fact they use Athletics made them 'unbalanced.' The general consensus was that the short range, relatively low base Damage, and Defense penalty balanced things out.<br /> <br /> Archery, as mentioned by others, has many of the advantages of firearms, such as long distance and burst fire. What we would like to have a firm answer on is the dicepool used for 'base' archery attacks. Our closest hint is the crossbow, which uses Dexterity+Firearms. Is this universal? Or does the dicepool for archery literally depend on the Style you're using? As a few others mentioned, archery lacks many of the disadvantages of thrown weapons, hence giving them Athletics for their dice pool potentially pushes it into overpowered territory. A long range weapon, capable of firearm-like damage, whose governing skill also boosts your Defense? Why would you choose to use a firearm over a bow, in that case? Unless there's something else I'm missing.<br /> <br /> Dicepools aside, the archery Styles themselves are great. I'm glad to see the return of the Iaijutsu Style. Have I mentioned how much I love the Thrown Weapons Styles? 'Many Blades, One Throw' gives us the long awaited ability to thrown multiple weaponized cards ala Gambit, while I appreciate how there's an alternate Style more focused on the sleight of hand/accuracy angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:31:26-07:00","id":446839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alisa180</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446705#post446705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this universal? Or does the dicepool for archery literally depend on the Style you're using?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I felt it was a good middle ground. It depends on how you're using the bow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:40:13-07:00","id":446846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446839#post446839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. I felt it was a good middle ground. It depends on how you're using the bow.</div> </div> </div> </div> Er, sorry if I'm asking a stupid question, but what if you don't have a Fighting Style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:20:02-07:00","id":446899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446846#post446846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Er, sorry if I'm asking a stupid question, but what if you don't have a Fighting Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ultimately what I was asking as well. But the implication seems to be, as he says, that it depends on how you're using the bow. Strength+Athletics and Dexterity+Firearms are both valid archery combat dicepools whether or not you have a Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4917-alisa180","name":"Alisa180","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:13:26-07:00","id":446977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=445479#post445479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can't because each Merit unlocks a new grappling maneuver in addition to the default list, so these are controlled by the grappling rules, which state 1 maneuver unless you score an exceptional success. This may be worth clarifying through.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you can combine grappling maneuvers with non grappling maneuvers, but not other grappling maneuvers? <br /> <br /> That's a little odd. Why is it easier to combine a boxing maneuver with wrestling than another wrestling maneuver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T05:04:56-07:00","id":447518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446977#post446977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can combine grappling maneuvers with non grappling maneuvers, but not other grappling maneuvers?<br /> <br /> That's a little odd. Why is it easier to combine a boxing maneuver with wrestling than another wrestling maneuver?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because you also cannot combine already existing grapple maneuvers. I cannot decide to take your weapon and restrain you at the same time for example. Grapple maneuvers are special actions, of which you can choose one when you win a grapple roll (or two when you roll and exceptional success).<br /> <br /> It is important here to distinguish grappling maneuvers from fighting style maneuvers of a grappling fighting style. As fighting style maneuvers are mostly action modifiers, they can in a lot of cases be combined with each other and with normal actions. So as long as a grappling fighting style maneuver is not the addition of an actual grappling maneuver, it can be combined with grappling maneuvers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":".  Grammar 03-18-2015, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:44:26-07:00","id":447670,"title":"","content":"I have a question: when using Boxing or other Style techniques that deal bashing automatically, like Whirlwind Strike from GMC, what happens if you were to combine it with a weapon that you can use Brawl with (punch daggers or brass knuckles), or have an ability that turns your hands into lethal weapons (Martial Arts Style 4 or 5).<br /> <br /> Would the damage be lethal in that situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:35:15-07:00","id":447938,"title":"","content":"I'd like it if the &quot;multiple attacks/targets&quot; maneuvers were harmonized to use a common-ish system; I think having a single guideline for &quot;How this sort of thing works&quot; would save a lot of book-checking at the table. We already have Autofire as our rules example of multiple targets, so I'd be inclined to make it the standard - you can attack X targets and suffer a -1 penalty for each target after the first.<br /> <br /> I think this is what we have listed for multiple targets:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Combat Archer 3: </b>Uses medium burst autofire rules.<br /> <b>Iajutsu 3: </b>Attack up to [Dexterity] targets, no apparent penalty. (Could be a &quot;medium burst autofire melee attack.&quot;)<br /> <b>Staff Fighting 4: </b>Attack all opponents &quot;in melee range&quot;, -1 penalty per target, but autohit any foe that attempts(? attempted?) a hand-to-hand attack that turn.<br /> <b>Alternate Thrown Weapons 3</b>: Attack up to [Dexterity] targets(?), -1 penalty per target. The penalty is &quot;per projectile&quot; but the text reads &quot;multiple targets&quot; so I assume this is one strike per target (as I think we're not returning to the multiple attacks on a single target scenario.)<br /> <b>Two-Weapon Fighting 4: </b>Split your attack pool between two targets and suffer a -2 penalty to each attack.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:09:49-07:00","id":448429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=446977#post446977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So you can combine grappling maneuvers with non grappling maneuvers, but not other grappling maneuvers?<br /> <br /> That's a little odd. Why is it easier to combine a boxing maneuver with wrestling than another wrestling maneuver?</div> </div> </div> </div>The term &quot;maneuver&quot; does not mean the same thing in the context of the list of things you can do while grappling as it does when describing the benefits of a Fighting Style Merit. The exceptions are those Merits that *explicitly* add an additional maneuver to the repertoire, which then become additional possible grappling results. The combat rules are clear about how many grappling maneuvers you can inflict on an opponent.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Storytelling is not a d20-style system where words have arbitrary meanings based on game system templates. Unless the text calls out something and labels it as a tag/template its meanings are in normal English and context-driven, not hard-coded.<br /> <br /> As for combining boxing and wrestling there are many cases where it works (such as MMA clinch work) but for the most part, boxing is hitting with Brawl and grappling is applying grappling maneuvers with Brawl, so they don't usually work together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T02:55:29-07:00","id":448963,"title":"","content":"If grabbing and other stuff is so incompatible, then the example of doing something else while putting someone in a headlock is a pretty damn bad example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 03-19-2015, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T22:49:24-07:00","id":450188,"title":"","content":"<b>Kiai</b><br /> O - This adds a diceroll without much thematic benefit. This is going to be one of those things that are either disappointing to use, or the person twinks this one thing out and it's devastating. Swingy mechanics like this encourage a type of min-maxing that isn't always helpful for your game and community. That said, I do /like/ the idea of Kiai 1 being effectively &quot;willpower, but better.&quot;<br /> OO - Easily trading turns is usually a bad mechanic because of how common the PCs vs 1 Enemy is and how valuable a PC's turn is in relation to an antagonist. You're ultimately saying, &quot;as a common mode of combat, your character easily makes nothing happen.&quot; I'd pick another condition. Alternatively, limit its uses per scene (beyond the willpower cost).<br /> OOO - The diceroll feels supliferous. This mechanic is also competing with Iron Skin.<br /> Overall: The concept is sound, the mechanics need new a new direction in some places. While I don't avoid extra dicerolls at all costs, I try to avoid them if I can because I feel they slow down play, but that may be a style thing. Oh! There should definately be something in here to negate wound penalties. Possibly any time someone uses one of these abilities, or maybe during any turn they spend willpower as long as they do a Kiai shout.<br /> <br /> <b>Kino Mutai</b><br /> O - +2B feels strong. But sure. I would totally love if this was written in such a way as to be compatable with supernatural (Vampire) biting, as a personal note.<br /> OO - I don't know what the &quot;Agony&quot; tilt is or what it does, so I can't really comment. As long as that checks out, this dot is cool. Agony is an awesome name.<br /> OOO - Ow. I like it. I'm not sure being blind actually impact grapple rolls? Not sure there, that could use some clarity. Also needs to specify one or two eyes.<br /> OOOO - Also ow.<br /> Overall: I am sadface my vampire or werewolf can't use this so much! I like the visceral feel and presentation of the style. Mechanics are probably circling about where they should be.<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts</b><br /> O - Needs shorter wording. It's solid, if a bit strong. &quot;1B&quot; should be &quot;1 Damage&quot; or similar, because lethal unarmed attacks are possible and someone will make that mistake.<br /> OO - This is basically +3 dice when performing a called shot (eyes). Concept is solid.<br /> OOO - I'd like the feel of this mechanic. I have no idea how strong it is, though. Mostly it feels more like an excuse to pull your punches without willpower cost or down an enemy and save some of the damage for the next enemy.<br /> OOOO - I like this. Consider damage as opposed to successes.<br /> OOOOO - This is not clearly written and honestly just isn't as useful as a flat +2 damage. Also feels more &quot;defensive style&quot;-y.<br /> Overall: All of these descriptions are /way/ too long, but I'm assuming that's a first draft thing. Most of it is solid. The fifth dot is the only one I'd consider doing serious work on, with an eye on the third dot during playtesting to see what actually happens when it's at the table. Everything will need a tuning and balance pass. Not sure why this isn't its own separate style.<br /> <br /> <b>Mounted Combat</b><br /> O - Yup. Feels standard and expected. May want to also have it improve Defense against attacks that'd knock her off. Heck, I'd be willing to make it just not need rolls to stay mounted unless in response to an attack.<br /> OO - I feel like this will never come up, but I also feel like Mounted Combat will never come up, so...<br /> OOO - I feel like this and the prior maneuver don't belong in the same fighting style. It's good, though, and a reason to take Mounted Combat.<br /> OOOO - See all prior comments about animals attacking during combat.<br /> Overall: Not going to lie, I may not be the best reviewer of this. Mounted Combat feels very out of genre for most of World of Darkness (historical settings aside) and this style isn't doing anything to convince me it'd be a good addition. That said, I recognize my own bias here.<br /> <br /> <b>Powered Projectile</b><br /> O - It's a tax, but it's needed so the player(s) go &quot;okay we're suspending disbelief on this guy reloading this giant crossbow.&quot;<br /> OO - Conceptually this is a bit eye-roll-y and I don't like it. It feels more 'meh' and stupid than cool and cinematic, but that's an opinion thing. Mechanics definitely need to be simpler. Reflexive action. Diceroll. Done. Forget the size and distance moved and etc.<br /> OOO - &quot;Next attack&quot; wut. Does this take an action? If so, this needs to be combined with an Aim action at minimum. If it's on the turn you fire... still feels weak for a no-defense 3-dot maneuver.<br /> OOOO - I like the idea of this but the mechanics need some pretty heavy polishing.<br /> Overall: Crossbows, slings, and blowguns are extremely different weapons and I have no idea why they are being lumped together. The only one that's actually powered is the crossbow. Otherwise it's pretty solid style, but doesn't wow me too much. I'd like to see it brought to five dots with one more pizzaz-y maneuver (either before or after Skewer).<br /> <br /> <b>Spear and Bayonet</b><br /> O - I don't see this coming up too much, but it's in theme so I like it anyways.<br /> OO - Hrm... Jury is out on this one. The name doesn't fit the mechanics, so some dissonance there. Unsure on game balance.<br /> OOO - I feel like this is a weird place for this mechanic. I mean it sort of fits, but it's just &quot;why here?&quot; I feels pretty generic.<br /> Overall: I kind of want a basic, solid, maro-esque experience from a Spear based fighting style, but this feels a bit too bland and thrown together.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope these are helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T08:58:22-07:00","id":450494,"title":"","content":"<b>Staff</b><br /> O - Feels appropriate and thematic. I like it.<br /> OO - Hrm. To be clear, this is a Disarm that ignores Defense (replacing it with the roll)? Not sure how I feel about that from a balance standpoint. I feel like that's a 3+ dot maneuver that should cost willpower or defense or something.<br /> OOO - I like this too, in concept. May want it to need to inflict damage.<br /> OOOO - How does this work with Defense? Highest? I'm sketchy on this being a thing. It should probably cost willpower to prevent spamming (there is no reason to /not/ use it).<br /> Overall: Well thought out style that fits the image of a 'staff wielder' in my mind. Good job.<br /> <br /> <b>Staff [ALTERNATIVE]</b><br /> O - I'm okay with this. Another thing to consider is to let the defense bonus apply against things with a bigger size.<br /> OO - Feels strong for a two-dot maneuver.<br /> OOO - Hrm... not sure which Leg Sweep I like more.<br /> OOOO - Feels appropriate. Does this onyl apply to people when they first come in, or if they stay in? &quot;Vortex of Doom&quot; Hehe.<br /> OOOOO - I'm not sure I like mechanics that take away the tactical decision of whether or not to Dodge. Good direction, but I'd divorce it from the dodge mechanic.<br /> Overall: Both staff styles are about the same. I think in the end the best result can be found by combining the two and using ideas from both.<br /> <br /> <b>Strength Performance</b><br /> O - Sure.<br /> OO - This is awesome and I absolutely love it. When I play a physical character who is not Jackie Chan this is the kind of stuff I want to do.<br /> OOO - This is one of those things that is going to sit on someone's character sheet for half a year, then they /finally/ get a chance to use it and they jump for joy. I feel like you could stop the description at quadruple the weight he can move and a page reference.<br /> OOOO - Do not like. It's boring for a capstone and will contribute to power creep too much. Its raw +2 Damage on all attacks aspect with no cost is no good, IMO.<br /> Overall: The two and three dot are awesome and make me jump for joy. This is a type of character I commonly play (currently built with Parkour and Demolisher) and I'm glad to see it get more support.<br /> <br /> <b>Systema</b><br /> O - Feels complicated and huge given what it does and it being a one-dot merit. But I think that's a presentation thing. The mechanics are fine.<br /> OO - Good enough.<br /> OOO - I really like this, and it's in line with Street Fighting.<br /> Overall: Two dot may need some work. Other than that it looks spot on.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrown Weapons</b><br /> O - Nice tone setter, I like it.<br /> OO - I don't think too many Size 1 weapons /have/ an initiative penalty.<br /> OOO - This kind of clashes with the one dot's feel, but I guess that's okay given the breadth of concepts being represented here.<br /> OOOO - Feels underwhelming.<br /> Overall: Starts off great, but the 2+ dots are really not getting me excited.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrown Weapons [ALTERNATE]</b><br /> O - This is pretty overpowered. Keep the other one. Maybe turn the other's second dot into a flat initiative increase or something.<br /> OO - This feels like a bow or crossbow maneuver. Not a throwing-knife maneuver. This maneuver makes no sense with most of the things you are going to throw.<br /> OOO - No multiple attacks like that please. Maybe let you use a Medium Burst or something by sacrificing defense.<br /> Overall: Not a fan of this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Two Weapon Fighting</b><br /> O - Sounds legit.<br /> OO - Also looks solid and appropriate.<br /> OOO - Excellent way to handle the multiple attacks thing.<br /> OOOO - This is pretty useless, given how Defense works.<br /> Overall: A nice solid take on two weapon fighting, a normally icky subject in RPGs. A lot of ways this could have turned out bad from word one. Good job. On a balance note, you may want to move away from using equipment bonuses. That can start stacking pretty badly when you start including supernatural elements that improve equipment bonuses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-20-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:40:42-07:00","id":450531,"title":"","content":"It's been talked about a little bit, but I feel like Punch Drunk is really worrying from a design stand point. As was mentioned, it allows for a normal human to take four hellfire missiles before going down, and works much more effectively and convincingly if limited to only bashing attacks as proposed. This in turn fits with the general shift in GMC to Lethal damage being a bit of a bigger deal.<br /> <br /> However my bigger concern, as the author of that merit said himself, is that it was balanced without supernaturals in mind... which is another point of contention for me. All of the supernaturals will draw from this book if the storytellers allow it, as all of them are at heart humans. It may be impossible to think of all the permutations for abuse from every supernatural splat there is, but a drawback as weak as &quot;doubled healing times&quot; is effortlessly overcome by even the base abilities of pretty much every supernatural I can think of - except maybe changelings.<br /> <br /> I like many of the merits here, but worry that the more you scale up everyone and everything the less it feels like a world of darkness and the more it feels like angsty superheroes.<br /> <br /> ________<br /> <br /> That worry aside, my other comment is that At Any Cost feels a bit overpriced to me. Especially when compared to things like Meditative Mind and Support Network, which can both easily make back the experience spent on them due to saved integrity.<br /> <br /> The number of times I've been in a combat that inflicted more than one or two tilts on a character and lasted more than three rounds are nonexistent. Maybe scale the cost back to 2 dots and make the requirements 2 Resolve and 2 Composure respectively? That way there's more room to grow into the merit if the character chooses to invest further experience into those traits.<br /> <br /> I'd also remove the mention of an &quot;opponent&quot; from it, as that makes it feel more fighty than a merit that could just as easily serve any of the emergency first responders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:01:51-07:00","id":451364,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts on Punch Drunk.<br /> <br /> - If your ST is using hellfire missiles (or tank rounds) against human characters and not inflicting the damage as aggravated, your game is running in some kind of extreme action hero mode that WoD really doesn't cover.<br /> <br /> - Punch Drunk is not for supernatural creatures. Humans only. I'll amend the text to clarify this. If STs decide to allow supernatural characters to take the merit despite this, the ST assumes responsibility for the problems this causes her chronicle.<br /> <br /> - Punch Drunk's design space is intended to in some way emulate the action movie element where the Stallones and Schwarzneggers take bullets and blades and somehow, beyond the point where anyone else would have died, he somehow just keeps coming. The mooks keep shooting, but the action hero just refuses to die.<br /> <br /> - All things being equal, Punch Drunk extends the character's life by up to 4 turns. 4 turns in which her actions are degraded (she still suffers dice penalties), but she can still act. This is the point in the action movie where the bad guys call for the flamethrowers, or high explosives, or whatever. They try to take the fight to aggravated, because she will. not. die. At this point, smart characters either use their few extra turns to get to cover, or hope that their allies are close enough to find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:42:00-07:00","id":451377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anachronistic Jam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=450531#post450531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been talked about a little bit, but I feel like Punch Drunk is really worrying from a design stand point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't let first drafts worry you. Please. <br /> <br /> The notes have been noted. I'll be keeping the various points in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T18:22:40-07:00","id":453509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=451364#post451364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Punch Drunk's design space is intended to in some way emulate the action movie element where the Stallones and Schwarzneggers take bullets and blades and somehow, beyond the point where anyone else would have died, he somehow just keeps coming. The mooks keep shooting, but the action hero just refuses to die.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.history.army.mil/moh/\" target=\"_blank\">Not just action movie heroes, it happens in real life, too.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:33:09-07:00","id":453651,"title":"","content":"So one thing I haven't seen people talk about much is how the new styles interact with the existing ones. Given that hybrid styles are intended to be a possibility I felt this was worth exploring so I did some research <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> These are organized first by tag, then by dot level. I\u2019m just going to name and give my assessment, since everything is either in the Fighting Style section of the GMC rules update or Hurt Locker Styles doc I won\u2019t bother with a more comprehensive cross reference atm. Will attempt to keep them in the order listed, no promises.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Striking Styles</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> One Dot </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts: Focused Attack:</b> Solid foundational one dot. Reducing penalty to hit specified target by 1 and armor by 1 potentially useful for almost any follow up</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Unarmed Defense: Like a Book: </b>Too situational. +2 defense is great if your character is a professional martial artist in a ring fight. Falls apart as soon as somebody pulls a knife or facing multiple opponents. Or multiple opponents with knives. A bonus you lose when things get *more* dangerous isn\u2019t helpful.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boxing:</b> <b>Head Protection: </b>Much like previous maneuver, not a huge fan. Not bad, but not great.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts(HLA): Leg Kick: </b>Great 1 dot move. Probably my favorite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Clinch Strike:</b> Listed as a Striking Merit, wouldn\u2019t use it as one. *Would* use as grappling merit, which it also is. Will return to in grappling section.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Two Dot </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts: Defensive Strike:</b> Good, not great. Useful for sizing up an opponent or when stalling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Unarmed Defense: Studied Style:</b> Meh. Only really relevant if facing more than one opponent. Still too situational </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boxing: Defensive Jab: </b>Great move. Might be *too* powerful if abilities that modify unarmed damage include it</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts(HLA): Cutting Elbow: </b>Interesting move! I like it for flavor, mechanics seem solid</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boot Party:</b> I see why this is a Striking maneuver but I don\u2019t see much use for it since there aren\u2019t any striking maneuvers that make inflicting Knockdown particularly easy. I could see it having and being used in Street and/or Grappling tags however.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Headbutt:</b> Interesting idea, mechanics are a little weird. I know stun locking is a concern but I feel like this could be handled with a normal attack roll and some modifiers. Might take this for fun if I had extra points on a street fighting type, but not as a core skill.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Three Dot </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts: Whirlwind Strike: </b>Similar to Defensive Jab. Would be interesting to have a character with both</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Unarmed Defense:</b> Redirect: This is where unarmed defense finally gets good. This skill is cool and fun, albeit not much use 1v1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boxing: Knockout Artist:</b> This is a solid ability. Stun is a powerful tilt and making it slightly easier to inflict is nice. Still requires a 4 damage hit though, so while good it wouldn\u2019t be my first pick.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts(HLA): Trapping:</b> This is a strange one and I\u2019m trying to understand where I would want to use it. Against an armored opponent, or as a setup for trying to Stun? It feels like the sort of thing you could use really effectively once and then opponents would learn to break contact before the other shoe dropped.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ground and Pound:</b> Much like Boot Party and Clinch Strike I don\u2019t see this making much sense in a Striking Style but Grappling and Street have great use for it</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Hip Drop: </b>Hip Drop is a really interesting case. Under normal circumstances it doesn\u2019t offer much, but it gets incredibly powerful if you have Touch of Death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Four Dot </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts: The Hand as Weapon:</b> This would be a really good merit if The Touch of Death didn\u2019t exist. However, in the new system there\u2019s very little reason to make your fists 0 lethal weapons when you can use this slot for another skill and make them +2 lethal as the capstone anyway.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Unarmed Defense: Joint Strike:</b> A contested Strength + Brawl roll from a style that emphasizes Dex isn\u2019t the greatest idea, especially since failure means you take damage like normal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boxing: Combination Blows:</b> This is interesting and potentially fairly powerful. Boxers will always have at least two dice, and may have as many as four at character creation. Typically this averages out to a +1 damage but I kind of like the variable damage aspect. A good pick.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts(HLA): Inch Force:</b> This is a solid defense against enemy grapplers, which are potentially quite dangerous under the new rules. Situational, but potentially a life-saver.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Five Dot </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts: The Touch of Death:</b> Incredibly hard to justify not taking this. Very powerful merit.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Unarmed Defense: Like The Breeze:</b> I was wrong, there is a good way to set up for those \u201cif opponent is prone\u201d moves. Cool Maneuver, satisfying pacifist type move.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boxing: Out for the Count: </b>Dealing enough damage to stun is still tough, but if you do the fight is over. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Martial Arts(HLA): High Momentum Strike:</b> Another possible source of Knockdown, or bonus damage. This isn\u2019t a bad move but others provide easier/more reliable means of achieving what it provides. Probably the weakest overall capstone.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My overall thoughts on a hybrid Striking Style: Focused attack or Leg Kick; Defensive Jab; Hip Drop; Combination Blows; and The Touch of Death. Defensive Combat: Brawl is a must, and Fighting Finesse: Striking allows me to make a str 2 dex 4 sta 2 martial artist who can wreak havoc with only 8 merit dots invested. Granted that\u2019s 1 more than a character gen mortal gets but still, not a bad investment if we\u2019re playing a slightly higher powered game. Alternatively, str 3 dex 3. Spare merit dots would go to inch force, knockout artist and out for the count, in that order. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Grappling! I\u2019m just going to list these by name, Grappling and Grappling Alt are easy to find but there are a ton of loose ones all over the place, sorry.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">One Dot</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Sprawl:</b> Solid, but kind of worrying. So many grappling merits are based on going prone that this means anyone with a one dot merit can make large sections of the style much harder to use. Do two characters with Sprawl remain standing during a grapple until one of them passes out or breaks free? This might need some weird house ruling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Standing Throw:</b> Hell yeah. This is a set up for most of what follows. Great one dot.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tuska Ate: </b>Pretty sure that bonus applies to the roll, not as bonus successes. My only issue with this is that it means the player and ST has to track a bunch of modifiers. Grappling is different from normal combat, grappling with a weapon has special sub rules, and inflicting tilts is another layer of mechanics.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Clinch Strike:</b> Great one dot, my favorite of the options.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Two Dot</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Takedown:</b> I\u2019m not super clear on how this is different than Standing Throw? It deals damage and doesn\u2019t require you to establish a grapple first, but otherwise it seems exactly the same.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Small Joint Manipulation:</b> Don\u2019t know what the Agony Tilt is yet but this is cool</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ChokeHold:</b> A great way to non lethally dispatch weak opponents but it scales poorly against high stamina ones.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Boot Party:</b> Not technically a grappling move according to the tags. Really should be since it can work off Standing Throw/Takedown so well.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Headbutt:</b> Everything I said about this before still stands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Trunk Squeeze:</b> Similar concept to Choke Hold but I like the execution better. Combine with Positional Dominance and Clinch Strike for massive bashing in short order.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Three Dot</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Joint Lock:</b> Basically an upgrade to the Hold move, and a good one at that. Solid, and a prereq for some of the upper tier abilities. My feeling is that it effectively creates a grappling sub style, which I like. You can be really good at joint locks, or you can do other grappling moves.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ippon:</b> Upgrades Takedown. Good if you\u2019re using Takedown, not so much if you aren\u2019t. Takedown is a good move though.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ground and Pound:</b> A great way to follow up Takedown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Ground Fighter:</b> Probably a good idea if you\u2019re going to be elbow dropping on prone opponents.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Four Dot</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dynamic Guard:</b> Solid, not a whole lot to say about this. It does tend to reinforce my notion that going dex four with fighting finesse in the chosen style is the best way to get an edge in unarmed combat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Lock Flow:</b> Makes Joint Lock better.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Five Dot</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tap or Snap:</b> This is awesome</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Positional Dominance:</b> This is a nice damage bonus that works with any other grappling maneuver. As such it\u2019s fairly powerful but for a style capstone I think it\u2019s appropriate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My overall feeling on grappling is that there are a lot of viable options. Going for Tap or Snap, a Restrain move, simply wearing the person out with tons of damage, or trying to stun them by slamming on the ground are all possible. Of all the Fighting Styles Grappling is now the one that I feel has the most interesting choices.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Light Weapons: I\u2019m not going to do the same style writeup as I did for Grappling and Striking. I just don\u2019t see much in the way of possible synergies between the styles that currently use the tag. If anybody disagrees I would love to be proved wrong! That said I like Kiriage as a possible replacement third dot for Light Weapons. Feint is an interesting move but somewhat tricky to understand, and as near as I can tell is only really worth it if the opponent is heavily armored.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Heavy Weapons: This style needs some love. Most of the other existing styles have gotten a fair bit in the way of new options, but Heavy Weapons got almost nothing, with one notable exception that I will get to later. Yes, Armed Defense is tagged as a Heavy Melee style as well as a Light Melee style, but the two don\u2019t actually mix well at all. To use techniques from both a character needs strength, dex *and* stamina all at three, a literal impossibility at character creation and an expensive sink even for more advanced characters. What Heavy Weapons did get was Hip Drop, a terrifying prospect when combined with a Fireaxe. Just hope you don\u2019t miss. Speaking of missing, could we get an alternate first dot for the style? Sacrificing three dice for a +1 weapon bonus is not remotely a good trade. In a system where attack and defense values are usually pretty close, that represents a massive drop in accuracy, and since successes add to damage that +1 just balances out the average damage lost to the missing dice. It\u2019s a net loss every time.</span></span><br /> <br /> I may get to Street Fighting later. For now I think this wall of text is already pretty massive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:15:40-07:00","id":453722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=453509#post453509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.history.army.mil/moh/\" target=\"_blank\">Not just action movie heroes, it happens in real life, too.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Punch drunk seems more akin to going out in a <i>blaze of glory</i>, particularly if the point of reference is the Medal of Honor .<br /> <br /> Maybe the merit could be reworked to provide additional temporary health dots under certain &quot;heroic&quot; circumstances and/or free actions before having to make the required rolls after suffering from all your lethal wound boxes, at a cost of a Willpower point, or even a full Willpower dot. A more appropriate a drawback might be suffering a long-lasting or persisting Tilt or Condition, representing crippling injuries or psychological scarring. It would be sort of a poor man's (or mortal's) Vampire Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T00:05:52-07:00","id":453928,"title":"","content":"Maybe Punch Drunk should simply prevent a person from falling unconscious for [merit dots] turns once damage wraps around?<br /> That keeps them standing beyond where normal folks would pass out, and means they're not 'immune' to hellfire missiles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T05:32:24-07:00","id":454117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=451364#post451364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> - Punch Drunk is not for supernatural creatures. Humans only. I'll amend the text to clarify this. If STs decide to allow supernatural characters to take the merit despite this, the ST assumes responsibility for the problems this causes her chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think that mundane merits should be locked away from any of the templates. Part of the point of the templates is that they are still at heart or origin, human. Making mundane merits that the supernaturals can't take separates them mechanically from that and then also feels really weird when apparently normal humans have access to some sort of in-born heroism that can allow them to take leagues more punishment than the most durable promethean or resilient vampire.<br /> <br /> Particularly for such a low buy-in cost. Resolve 3, Composure 3 is pretty cheap for such a supposedly &quot;hero-locked&quot; ability, and only slightly above average, assuming humans average 2 in any stat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=451364#post451364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- If your ST is using hellfire missiles (or tank rounds) against human characters and not inflicting the damage as aggravated, your game is running in some kind of extreme action hero mode that WoD really doesn't cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the Hellfire missile example not being appropriate, I discuss Rules As Written when discussing design, not Rules As Intended. These rules are being put up explicitly for feedback and revision, so discussions on written rules are important I think. Sure, you could change it so that missiles deal Agg, but per RAW the following all do Lethal damage and would be protected against, including 2000 pound bombs (Armory p. 111), Rank 5 Entity blasts (GMC p.229), supernatural meteor strikes (Mummy, p. 130), and fires of all intensity (NWoD Core p.180). Changing the way that Lethal damage is applied as opposed to Aggravated damage would require a comprehensive overhaul nearly all of NWoD and NWoD2e combat mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you wanted a more relevant example I could have used a werewolf's talons, an eldritch creature's mauling, four consecutive car crashes. Take your pick, but singling out the fact that missiles are an absurd example is missing the entire point of the example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=453928#post453928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Punch Drunk should simply prevent a person from falling unconscious for [merit dots] turns once damage wraps around?<br /> That keeps them standing beyond where normal folks would pass out, and means they're not 'immune' to hellfire missiles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that really matches with the apparently intended role of the merit *and* could play nicely as a merit that works for templates as well as base mortals. Sure there are ways for abusing it, but not so locked-in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","user":"Anachronistic Jam","date":". 03-23-2015, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:08:45-07:00","id":454772,"title":"","content":"RAW (NWoD core) give STs discretion to apply massive damage sources against mortals as Aggravated. Providing an absurd example reduces the feedback's value. I provided clarifying points because it appeared you'd missed the point of the merit, and were playing the game in some kind of explosive splatter mode.<br /> <br /> Regardless, as David said, comments have been noted, and will be included in second draft review consideration. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:37:41-07:00","id":454855,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I am disturbed by the change in tone I am seeing here.<br /> <br /> I feel the current merits do not feel amenable to a horror game. I love the idea of giving players more options to how to play their characters, but I have two major issues: Some of these seem are too powerful. They appear to give the player more than just options, but a serious edge that removes some of the constrained nature of the game. These merits are empowering, and that is not a good thing. (I can &quot;project&quot; a field that makes people fight more fairly? That seems a little much.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. The way this is written worries me. The idea that having friends around to &quot;validate you&quot; will just make things better. The idea that if you watch a truly horrific (your friend getting eviscerated as you are mind raped) scene you can brush it off with some hugs and tea. The trauma and sanity loss are meant to be serious parts of this game handled maturely, and they seem to be getting downplayed. I think the power being given to the players sends the wrong message about what this game is and how to handle issues in your own life. You don't get better and you aren't supposed to. Things stick with you and take effort to deal with. Friends and loved ones are not there to validate you. They challenge you, support you, and lead by example. This is more than the stresses of a work day, these are horrors that threaten life and sanity.<br /> <br /> Now of course I do not want to be needlessly negative. I am just confused about what the overriding goal of this is. Honestly I think much of it could be fixed with phrasing, emphasizing that being a well rounded person can help ameliorate these issues though not eliminate them entirely. And isn't that what the mechanics are going for in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","user":"Mr. Feral","date":". 03-23-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:24:36-07:00","id":455815,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts, though I'm not totally sure how many of these fit what you're seeking MachineVI.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to see rules for characters developing, teaching, and adapting these fighting techniques. The mechanics are pretty good: some hiccups, sure, but those have essentially been addressed. Still would like to have a mechanical benefit to having a teacher who mastered a technique over one who kinda gets the point. I mean, a poor teacher hinders development, a mediocre teacher can generally help over none at all, but an excellent teacher can help you advance in leaps and bounds.<br /> <br /> Why focus on the therapist with a new merit when the key point is the coping mechanisms? Seems overly specific to me. A therapist is a councilor who aids a person in learning what they need to cope, so I would think treating them as a teacher who makes learning the merit (or merits) that permit coping would make more sense. Is the concern the sheer volume of merits that could arguably require? (an approach to containing could be to make a merit that applies to a specific trauma as selected on development.)<br /> <br /> &quot;Zanshin&quot; is often used specifically to refer to the state of mind <i>after</i> an attack, though I double-checked, and it does literally fit use as a more general awareness term as in Iaijutsu. Is that how the term is applied in iajutsu schools? I'm more familiar with it from in kendo, jodo, and aikido, and, for me, that term did not properly introduce the idea of the merit.<br /> <br /> Calling your generic striking art &quot;martial arts&quot; is even more generally confusing, I suspect.<br /> <br /> &quot;Boot Party&quot; called to mind <i>exactly</i> what you were intending.<br /> <br /> Transfer Maneuver is a good merit, and one that applies very well to ninjutsu and aikido, among others. Maybe mention that?<br /> <br /> The karmic burdened who become &quot;demons&quot; through combat would make a great template for such a book. Kinda hoping for those and berserks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T08:32:30-07:00","id":459025,"title":"","content":"I've finally done a more comprehensive examination of the normal, non-fighting-style merits and figured I would toss my thoughts up.<br /> <br /> - Air of Menace: My initial impression was that this costs the same, but is better and more wide-ranging than an intimidation specialty + area of expertise. However, the drawback is significant and forces a shift in the way any character with this merit is played. I really like that, it means that taking this merit is a meaningful choice that not everyone who picks up Intimidate would want to take. Honestly, this merit is excellently done in my opinion.<br /> <br /> - Cohesive Unit: This synergizes really dangerously with Inspiring and Small Unit Tactics... which, not exactly my cup of tea, but I can certainly appreciate the opening of this as an effective character build. It should be noted that this merit really needs to specify how often its bonuses can be utilized because that will significantly affect balance - and while you're at it, a penalty for a few rounds when most countermanding orders will be issued outside of combat is insignificant to the point of triviality, it's not a drawback in anything but name (especially because the bonus appears to apply to out-of-combat situations as well). I would personally suggest a drawback duration of &quot;one scene.&quot; to make it more meaningful and encourage those who take this merit to actually be tuned into the needs of their superiors.<br /> <br /> - Support Network MK I: I hate hate hate hate hate True Friend, as can be seen in my post against Sanctity of Merits, so can't provide meaningful feedback here.<br /> <br /> - Support Network MK II: Far too cheap for the benefit, and Mr. Feral has expressed the rest of my feelings regarding this merit.<br /> <br /> - Professional Therapist: See Mr. Feral's post, but I also think that this combined with Meditative mind makes for a character who will virtually never fail a breaking point.<br /> <br /> - Support Group, A.K.A Support Network MK III: See Mr. Feral's post again for issues with tone, not to mention once more how easily this merit will pay for itself now that experience costs are flat progression.<br /> <br /> - Torturer: How is this different than Vice-Ridden (GMC p. 153)? Does it stack? Can I have a character with three effective vices? If I fulfill my vice while torturing someone do I get 2 willpower for that action?<br /> <br /> - At Any Cost: I like it. It stands at the same tier as Hardy/Iron stamina for similar effect and cost. I'd only suggest, like them, making it a 1-3 dot merit, rather than a flat 3 dot.<br /> <br /> - Defender: The bonus willpower is a strange notion. How is it supposed to be denoted on a character sheet, or should you just make a mental note of it? That's a pretty trivial concern all things considered, but it's mostly by way of saying that I think there are more elegant ways to achieve this base effect without introducing &quot;temporary willpower&quot; as a mechanic. The writing is another weak point of this merit; it's just terribly dramatic and reading it leads me in mind of those marty-stue Lawful Good paladins of D&amp;D yesteryear. It feels written to suit an opera character.<br /> <br /> - Dominating Center Line: I like the idea, but once more it feels like a merit better covered by a specialty+area of expertise... and would probably occur more often. If they stack, then that gets a bit absurd and reinforces the notion of GMC as the game where two people wiff at each other until one miraculously succeeds on a chance die.<br /> <br /> - Know the Territory: Really nice, not gratuitously powerful, decent cost. I like it a great deal. My only concern is this line: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This prevents the enemy from escaping&quot; </span></span></span>when setting a trap. That needs a great deal of more detail, if not removed entirely.<br /> <br /> - Living With Death: I've always felt that AOAs were unimpressive for the cost of dropping your defense. It's nice to see a merit that makes them more worthwhile.<br /> <br /> - Mental Scarring: Nothing really to say mechanically, but I really like the emphasis on trauma being not the sort of thing you suck up and move on entirely from, that old scars can be reopened.<br /> <br /> - Power Object: This needs a new name, but I love its effects both in terms of benefits and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> - Master of the Mask: Another merit that is perfectly replicated at the same cost and no drawback by a specialty + area of expertise + interdisciplinary specialty. I like the idea, but again, unless it stacks with aforementioned combination, it's never going to be worth it for the drawback alone.<br /> <br /> - Aggressive Driving: The second dot should be resisted by the opponent's Drive, or wits+drive, not Defense. Especially because a fair number of characters take the relatively cheap option of having Defense operate off of Brawl or Weaponry. J-Turn I feel like should be contested, unless the wall of police cars behind you all magically vanish. Other than those concerns, I like it. It makes chases more engaging and is good without being unbeatable by those without it.<br /> <br /> - Body As A Weapon: I like it, but then, given my propensity for liking things with hefty drawbacks, is that any surprise?<br /> <br /> - Dirty Fighter: The description in the drawback should state &quot;know and care about his reputation.&quot; Just because people know about a reputation for dirty fighting doesn't automatically make them less trusted in other areas of their lives.<br /> <br /> - Drone Control: Where to begin? It's reaaaaally hard not to mock this merit mercilessly. It's awful. Where in NWoD is there the need to waste space and word-count on something better covered by obscure applications of the drive and/or computer skills? Where is the need for characters that sit passively removed from the threat? Play NWoD with all the fun and excitement of an actual drone operator! Days and days of boredom before melting unsuspecting enemies from distances too far to be detected! All the tension and horror of staring at a screen, unmoving for days!<br /> I'm sorry I can't give constructive feedback on this one because my only advice is to remove it entirely. If you are really interested in including rules for remote drones and robots, then make that an actual section of the rules, not a fighting style merit. That's like having a fighting style for carrier groups. I am being serious though. Could someone explain what this merit provides that would be worth the wordcount?<br /> <br /> - Fair Fighter: This merit is overpowered, undermines the tone of NWoD as well as the supposed idea behind Hurt Locker that combat is unpleasant and brutal, and has a drawback that barely deserves the name. For mortal characters, this has a surprising &quot;paladin aura&quot; vibe coming off of it in waves.<br /> <br /> - One-Handed Driving; This should have a mention of how it interfaces with Ambidexterity, but otherwise I like it.<br /> <br /> - Punch Drunk: My feelings on this are well documented and don't bear repeating.<br /> <br /> - Roadkill: Wow. Vicious. Not bad, selectively useful, and quite dangerous. All to the good I say. I mean evil. All to the evil.<br /> <br /> - Survivalist: Nice. Though I see a herald of the return of Page XX, its coming is nigh! Nigh I say! Woe to the unbelievers and those who have forgotten its glorious reign!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T11:23:06-07:00","id":459224,"title":"","content":"Okay, I noticed with the Deconstructing Fighting Styles rules that some folks are focusing more on the math-hammer of the WiP rules, than how the rules themselves actually work. I think actually looking at the rules intent over how expensive it does or doesn't make fighting styles will go a long way in actually understanding the potential in these rules. What follows is an example of my own personal interpretation of how these rules are supposed to work, which is based mostly off of how things are described and how certain merits have actually been implemented.<br /> <br /> First, though, I would like to explain that my interpretation of how this changes Fighting Styles, is each level is now treated as it's own individual 1 dot merit, but what the levels mean now is the same as before, i.e., how capable in the tagged style one actually is. However, in order to actually be that capable, you have to have a broader range of knowledge in lesser abilities, which is where the prerequisite dots element comes in. So, with that said, let's look at a step by step process of how I think this works with a grappling monkey.<br /> <br /> Okay, so going with Grappling as the example here; I am going to cater my grappler towards a series of throws and locks, mostly aimed at subduing, incapacitating, or damaging an opponent in debilitating ways. To start with, I need a level 1 maneuver, as I do not yet have any to draw off of to take any higher maneuvers. So I take Standing Throw. I now meet the prerequisites for a level 2 maneuver, so I take Takedown, as it's befitting the theme. I now have 2 dots within the grappling tag. Now, let's say that taking a level 3 maneuver to unlock the abilitiy to take further level 3's is actually the prerequisite. I buy the character Ippon, as the character meets the prerequisites for that particular manuever already. I now have access to further level 3 merits.<br /> <br /> So far I have 3 dots in fighting merits which are tagged grappling, and while I am now able to purchase future level 3 manuevers, that is as high as I can progress in grappling tagged merits until such a time as I get 6 dots spread across grappling tagged maneuvers and merits rated up to 3. So I buy the character Ground and Pound. Which instantly boosts his total dots to 6. I can now purchase maneuvers in the level 4 category.<br /> <br /> Given the access to level 4 maneuvers my character now has, I take the Dynamic Guard maneuver, but I also find the Joint Lock maneuver very fitting for the methodology I am creating. So I spend 1 exp on Dynamic Guard, another on Joint Lock, and since I feel that it is also fitting, I spend 1 exp on Clinch Strike, and another on Sprawl, so that people have a harder time using his own methods against him. This has thus raised my total dots in grappling tagged merits to 10. This thus allows me access to 5th level maneuvers.<br /> <br /> Given as there isn't much choice to draw from in the grappling tag, I simply take the Positional Dominance maneuver.<br /> <br /> And for anyone who wants to math hammer it, we can break it down like this. 1 (Standing Throw)+1 (Takedown) +1 (Ippon) +3 (Ground And Pound) +1 (Dynamic Guard) +1 (Joint Lock) +1 (Clinch Strike) +1 (Sprawl) +1 (Positional Dominance) = 11<br /> <br /> If this is indeed the intent of the writers, then I hope it hopes folks actually envision the new rules in execution. However, if I have in fact misinterpreted the rules, I apologize in advance for added confusion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T13:47:34-07:00","id":459361,"title":"","content":"I just want to note that I dislike split dice pools as a mechanic, I feel that a -2 penalty to the attack roll against multiple enemies is very fair, and I'm a big fan of melee style merits that help one fight through throngs of enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T21:37:40-07:00","id":459670,"title":"","content":"I really like this draft (the style tag option in particular is going to be incredibly helpful in reflecting different characters relationships to violence by customizing the way they fight to the kinds of violence they expect to deal with). That said, there are a couple ideas you might want to consider.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Air of Menace</b>- I am not sure if Intimidate dots should be the only resistance option as it seems to conflate courage with the ability to be scary. Maybe there should be an option for characters with high resolve and/or composure to resist it as well in at least certain situations?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Cohesive Unit</b>-- The wording makes it unclear how this would apply to groups with a rotating leadership system. Say you have a team with a rotating system of leadership based on task (e.g. one team member is in charge of matters relating to combat, another social/political maneuvering, a third research/investigation). Does this merit's benefits and drawback always apply or can they be dialed back when the member with this merit is not in charge of the given subject area?<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Dominating Center Line</b>- This is problematic because it means that the failure of someone higher in the initiative order can cause problems for people farther down that are not necessarily logical. I have played in games where rules like this were used and it made a lot of players (who were using similar fighting techniques) incredibly frustrated as they felt they were punished for the failures of the other characters.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>More options to help run away could be nice.</b> In games that I have run, the hardest thing about making violence real has been countering my players notion that the only viable outcomes of a fight are you kill your opponent or you lose. It would be nice to have a few more options to facilitate characters fighting to create a viable opening to escape (if say a PC is jumped by goons while investigating something odd a combat maneuver or two that imposed a tilt that aided escaping and penalized the targets chasing them would make a nice addition to the light melee, street, and striking styles). This would also have the advantage of creating more options to use the vehicle and chase rules (not to mention the safe place merit would come into its own as that hidey-hole could be more readily brought to bear) While <b>Avoidance</b> helps, it could use a 5th dot option to help with disengaging from combat altogether and does not provide options for the rest of the group to create their own break off the engagement space. If this could be done, it would make players deal with the consequences of choosing more lethal combat builds as they would now know they could have tried to avoid fighting in at least some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3406,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3406-jalrin","user":"jalrin","date":". 03-28-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3406-jalrin","name":"jalrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T11:19:50-07:00","id":462494,"title":"","content":"I know its not practical, but dual wielding pistols is something that should have a merit to do. Or should I just tweak the two weapon fighting style to do so?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:16:07-07:00","id":462946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=462494#post462494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its not practical, but dual wielding pistols is something that should have a merit to do. Or should I just tweak the two weapon fighting style to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a very specific thing that leaves World of Darkness territory for me. I'm not a sucker for realism here, but I do want to keep things feeling World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:50:38-07:00","id":463029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=462494#post462494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its not practical, but dual wielding pistols is something that should have a merit to do. Or should I just tweak the two weapon fighting style to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very easy custom Merit. I'd say 3 dots, allows you to use short burst, medium burst, and covering fire maneuvers with one semi-automatic firearm in each hand, using half the normal ammunition cost (rounding up if neccessary) from each. -2 to the attack roll if you don't have Ambidextrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T21:05:14-07:00","id":464243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=462946#post462946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a very specific thing that leaves World of Darkness territory for me. I'm not a sucker for realism here, but I do want to keep things feeling World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, although I for one wouldn't mind the return of combat hacks in hurt locker, with options for different modes from even deadlier to wuxia/gun fu, I'm not holding my breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:17:03-07:00","id":464649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=464243#post464243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, although I for one wouldn't mind the return of combat hacks in hurt locker, with options for different modes from even deadlier to wuxia/gun fu, I'm not holding my breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really allocated for space. While I'm not against it, we're way too far in for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:31:26-07:00","id":464657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=459224#post459224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I noticed with the Deconstructing Fighting Styles rules that some folks are focusing more on the math-hammer of the WiP rules, than how the rules themselves actually work. I think actually looking at the rules intent over how expensive it does or doesn't make fighting styles will go a long way in actually understanding the potential in these rules. What follows is an example of my own personal interpretation of how these rules are supposed to work, which is based mostly off of how things are described and how certain merits have actually been implemented.<br /> <br /> First, though, I would like to explain that my interpretation of how this changes Fighting Styles, is each level is now treated as it's own individual 1 dot merit, but what the levels mean now is the same as before, i.e., how capable in the tagged style one actually is. However, in order to actually be that capable, you have to have a broader range of knowledge in lesser abilities, which is where the prerequisite dots element comes in. So, with that said, let's look at a step by step process of how I think this works with a grappling monkey.<br /> <br /> Okay, so going with Grappling as the example here; I am going to cater my grappler towards a series of throws and locks, mostly aimed at subduing, incapacitating, or damaging an opponent in debilitating ways. To start with, I need a level 1 maneuver, as I do not yet have any to draw off of to take any higher maneuvers. So I take Standing Throw. I now meet the prerequisites for a level 2 maneuver, so I take Takedown, as it's befitting the theme. I now have 2 dots within the grappling tag. Now, let's say that taking a level 3 maneuver to unlock the abilitiy to take further level 3's is actually the prerequisite. I buy the character Ippon, as the character meets the prerequisites for that particular manuever already. I now have access to further level 3 merits.<br /> <br /> So far I have 3 dots in fighting merits which are tagged grappling, and while I am now able to purchase future level 3 manuevers, that is as high as I can progress in grappling tagged merits until such a time as I get 6 dots spread across grappling tagged maneuvers and merits rated up to 3. So I buy the character Ground and Pound. Which instantly boosts his total dots to 6. I can now purchase maneuvers in the level 4 category.<br /> <br /> Given the access to level 4 maneuvers my character now has, I take the Dynamic Guard maneuver, but I also find the Joint Lock maneuver very fitting for the methodology I am creating. So I spend 1 exp on Dynamic Guard, another on Joint Lock, and since I feel that it is also fitting, I spend 1 exp on Clinch Strike, and another on Sprawl, so that people have a harder time using his own methods against him. This has thus raised my total dots in grappling tagged merits to 10. This thus allows me access to 5th level maneuvers.<br /> <br /> Given as there isn't much choice to draw from in the grappling tag, I simply take the Positional Dominance maneuver.<br /> <br /> And for anyone who wants to math hammer it, we can break it down like this. 1 (Standing Throw)+1 (Takedown) +1 (Ippon) +3 (Ground And Pound) +1 (Dynamic Guard) +1 (Joint Lock) +1 (Clinch Strike) +1 (Sprawl) +1 (Positional Dominance) = 11<br /> <br /> If this is indeed the intent of the writers, then I hope it hopes folks actually envision the new rules in execution. However, if I have in fact misinterpreted the rules, I apologize in advance for added confusion!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was just curious, Machine/any developer in the know, is the above example what was intended with the rules, or not? So I have a better knowledge over what exactly we could be playtesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:35:54-07:00","id":465099,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain that each merit dot costs 1 xp but is worth its dot rating for the purposes of style progression. That way the old 1-2-3-4-5 styles still work exactly the same if you want them to. For my own theory crafting I've stuck to swapping around things of the same dot level for simplicity's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:42:45-07:00","id":465392,"title":"","content":"It was explained to me earlier in the thread after I asked a bunch of questions. Basically 1-5 is still just 5 experience. Even if you mix and match. If say you did light weapons style a 1-3, and style b 4 and 5, it would still be 5 exp. So your not buying a 1 dot merit, a 2 dot merit, a 3 dot merit, a 4 dot merit and a 5 dot merit(15 exp) your just buying 5 maneuvers (5xp) . Basically David explained that 1-5 is still just 5 exp. Even if you get it piecemeal/build-a-style way. Each maneuver is 1xp regardless of rating so long as you have the prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:34:56-07:00","id":465761,"title":"","content":"I loved there diversity of the merits, but I was wondering if there'd be any fighting styles based on computer warfare? Since control doesn't really cover the sort of hacking type attacks I was thinking about. I guess to go with that you'd need stats for companies etc, and then I'd worry about moving too close to shadow run.<br /> <br /> Also, I suppose we haven't covered items yet, but surely there're virus and having services for sale somewhere in that book? <br /> <br /> As a final note the falconry style is epic. Love it. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T01:38:07-07:00","id":465794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=465761#post465761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved there diversity of the merits, but I was wondering if there'd be any fighting styles based on computer warfare? Since control doesn't really cover the sort of hacking type attacks I was thinking about. I guess to go with that you'd need stats for companies etc, and then I'd worry about moving too close to shadow run.<br /> <br /> Also, I suppose we haven't covered items yet, but surely there're virus and having services for sale somewhere in that book?<br /> <br /> As a final note the falconry style is epic. Love it. :-D</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I can make room for something like that. I have an idea. It might not go in Hurt Locker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T04:26:06-07:00","id":465914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=465794#post465794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me see if I can make room for something like that. I have an idea. It might not go in Hurt Locker.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds promising. No need to put it into HL if it won't fit. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T05:56:16-07:00","id":465985,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I am skeptical of playing up the prevalence of technology in WoD. To me it feels like it detracts from the personal experience necessary to a horror game. I build my games around the idea that players will have to be more directly involved in their interactions. Computer warfare is more seems a better fit in Shadowrun because the game is built around technology. Really with the powers and fear effects in this game I am starting to feel it might be more appropriate to just have early nineties as the implied setting to rid players of the notion that they can circumvent their problems with a hacking attempt or something on their phone. It's one thing to come up with a creative solution to a situation, but at some point the prevalence of tech (especially if the game was not built with it in mind) starts to feel too easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T06:53:24-07:00","id":466019,"title":"","content":"As a security focussed Software Engineer and former System Administrator, I have a fundamental dislike for all things &quot;hacking&quot; it isn't really an actively contested thing like they show in the movies. Some things can be, like any remote Denial of Service. But you're trying to breach network security? it's highly unlikely anyone is on the other end watching you. Contested hacking is for the movies. Most of the time it's either A hacker can't get in security too good, or B hacker gets in &quot;organization&quot; finds out later or they don't. It's basically more of a question of did you get in? how well, did you cover your tracks? I'd say it's an extended roll, and requires 1 exceptional success that can be applied to covering your tracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:09:07-07:00","id":467230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=465985#post465985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I am skeptical of playing up the prevalence of technology in WoD. To me it feels like it detracts from the personal experience necessary to a horror game. I build my games around the idea that players will have to be more directly involved in their interactions. Computer warfare is more seems a better fit in Shadowrun because the game is built around technology. Really with the powers and fear effects in this game I am starting to feel it might be more appropriate to just have early nineties as the implied setting to rid players of the notion that they can circumvent their problems with a hacking attempt or something on their phone. It's one thing to come up with a creative solution to a situation, but at some point the prevalence of tech (especially if the game was not built with it in mind) starts to feel too easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This book is definitely not set in the 1990s. <br /> <br /> I don't think I've ever had the problem you speak of. But I'll keep it in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T05:13:18-07:00","id":467235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=466019#post466019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a security focussed Software Engineer and former System Administrator, I have a fundamental dislike for all things &quot;hacking&quot; it isn't really an actively contested thing like they show in the movies. Some things can be, like any remote Denial of Service. But you're trying to breach network security? it's highly unlikely anyone is on the other end watching you. Contested hacking is for the movies. Most of the time it's either A hacker can't get in security too good, or B hacker gets in &quot;organization&quot; finds out later or they don't. It's basically more of a question of did you get in? how well, did you cover your tracks? I'd say it's an extended roll, and requires 1 exceptional success that can be applied to covering your tracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Most everything in World of Darkness is &quot;for the movies&quot;. It7s about horror fiction, which feels real to the casual observer. But ultimately isn't. It's about the fiction. <br /> <br /> I doubt we'll do anything extensive. This isn't supposed to be Minority Report or anything like that. But I do have a passing familiarity with computer boxes and things. I successfully updated iTunes earlier today. <br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I get your point. As a writer, when I see movies about writers, I have that &quot;they're getting it totally wrong, that's not how publishing works!&quot; But, that's really the rub. <br /> <br /> Ironically, I won an award for something I wrote for Shadowrun. The public response was that the tech level was too low, and I hampered the ability to solve everything with technology. Fun times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T06:32:24-07:00","id":467302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=467235#post467235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Most everything in World of Darkness is &quot;for the movies&quot;. It7s about horror fiction, which feels real to the casual observer. But ultimately isn't. It's about the fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>didn't you just use some inverted argument to say no to dual wielding pistols? (which I totally want for Demon).<br /> <br /> If you're going for Gritty, I think the real worlds view is more so. Security people have to get it right the first time, after that, attackers can attack you until you fall. Maybe if you're looking at contest it could be defender rolls extended first to set up their network, applications, etc, their total success are the roll the attacker has to beat. The attacker then can roll to beat that, if they do, their in (again exceptional success to cover tracks).<br /> <br /> Me personally? I'd be more interested in rules/discussion of what you can do once you've successfully hacked the electronic device. In the real world, the NSA monitors everything. In the real world our cars now have wirelessly communicating components that can be hacked (seriously, I want rules for this, your brakes are mine). In the real world a hacker can steal your identity and ruin your credit or leach money for a long time (removal of resource dots). In the real world people can post your private photos on the internet or use them for blackmail. You can hijack someone's webcam and constantly transmit when the laptops on. The NSA (allegedly) compromised (compromise is real) the firmware on the hard drives to circumvent harddrive encryption.<br /> <br /> Please, whatever you do don't let the real world be more gritty than the world of darkness.","signature":"<hr 