ous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:19:40-07:00","id":467827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=467817#post467817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oookay...<br /> <br /> I think what he means is that, if you've got a Demon character who wants to go guns akimbo, Interlocks provide a system for creating custom powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. 10 characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:39:49-07:00","id":468023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=467302#post467302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> didn't you just use some inverted argument to say no to dual wielding pistols? (which I totally want for Demon).<br /> <br /> If you're going for Gritty, I think the real worlds view is more so. Security people have to get it right the first time, after that, attackers can attack you until you fall. Maybe if you're looking at contest it could be defender rolls extended first to set up their network, applications, etc, their total success are the roll the attacker has to beat. The attacker then can roll to beat that, if they do, their in (again exceptional success to cover tracks).<br /> <br /> Me personally? I'd be more interested in rules/discussion of what you can do once you've successfully hacked the electronic device. In the real world, the NSA monitors everything. In the real world our cars now have wirelessly communicating components that can be hacked (seriously, I want rules for this, your brakes are mine). In the real world a hacker can steal your identity and ruin your credit or leach money for a long time (removal of resource dots). In the real world people can post your private photos on the internet or use them for blackmail. You can hijack someone's webcam and constantly transmit when the laptops on. The NSA (allegedly) compromised (compromise is real) the firmware on the hard drives to circumvent harddrive encryption.<br /> <br /> Please, whatever you do don't let the real world be more gritty than the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to do a book about this stuff. I've actually pitched one more than a few times. <br /> <br /> This kind of commentary is pretty close to my heart. I have some material lined up that might exhibit it, or it might fall flat, depending on your opinion. <br /> <br /> And yes. I did, actually. Because &quot;fiction&quot; does not mean &quot;all fiction&quot;. To me, certain affordances in simplifying the role of technology in stories can be valuable. Emulating Hellraiser 8 is a reasonable fiction choice to me here (I liked Hellraiser 8, don't judge). Emulating Equilibrium isn't really. Not to me.<br /> <br /> I hope that clarifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:32:59-07:00","id":468059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468023#post468023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes. I did, actually. Because &quot;fiction&quot; does not mean &quot;all fiction&quot;. To me, certain affordances in simplifying the role of technology in stories can be valuable. Emulating Hellraiser 8 is a reasonable fiction choice to me here (I liked Hellraiser 8, don't judge). Emulating Equilibrium isn't really. Not to me.<br /> <br /> I hope that clarifies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on . . . are you telling us that Hurt Locker will not include an indispensable &quot;Tetragrammaton Cleric&quot; template and detailed Gun Kata merits?!?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess I'll just have to cross Hurt Locker off my &quot;must buy&quot; list and re-appropriate those funds for the next supplement of <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katanas &amp; Trenchcoats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:29:48-07:00","id":468080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468059#post468059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hold on . . . are you telling us that Hurt Locker will not include an indispensable &quot;Tetragrammaton Cleric&quot; template and detailed Gun Kata merits?!?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess I'll just have to cross Hurt Locker off my &quot;must buy&quot; list and re-appropriate those funds for the next supplement of <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Katanas &amp; Trenchcoats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I support this message. <br /> <br /> If anyone here hasn't already seen Katanas and Trenchcoats, a number of our awesome writers worked on it, and all the proceeds go to the Seattle Children's Hospital. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://somanykatanas.com\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://somanykatanas.com\" target=\"_blank\"> Katanas &amp; Trenchcoats </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://somanykatanas.com\" target=\"_blank\"> http://somanykatanas.com </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Live the Dream of '90s Roleplaying </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:41:17-07:00","id":468087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468080#post468080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I support this message.<br /> <br /> If anyone here hasn't already seen Katanas and Trenchcoats, a number of our awesome writers worked on it, and all the proceeds go to the Seattle Children's Hospital.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://somanykatanas.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://somanykatanas.com</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope you can at least assure us that Hurt Locker will include mechanics for angst-filled flashbacks and heroic theme music. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for choosing between Hurt Locker and Katanas &amp; Trenchcoats, I'm confident that it's not a situation of &quot;there can be only one.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:04:19-07:00","id":468350,"title":"","content":"One concern I have regards the sheer disproportion I am seeing in power between these merits and the ones in the GMC. As opposed to simply providing more options, several of these seem to me to be too good to pass up. While Small Unit Tactics and Inspiring provided a nice edge in combat but were no means definitive, a party with a social tank utilizing Cohesive Unit can expect to drastically outperform a party which is even on average better at what they do. I worry this will create a &quot;everyone uses it or no one does&quot; mentality among groups when it comes to this book, limiting options rather than granting them.<br /> <br /> To continue with the above example, another concern is that with merits like it and Know the Territory mental and social characters now are able to &quot;double up&quot;, so to speak: i.e. using their non-physical skills and abilities to become combat powerhouses. This feels more apt for a game like DnD or Exalted (switching out your attack skill, using certain special martial arts) rather than NWoD to me. While there have always been things like Fighting Finesse (though that was with another physical attribute) and supernatural activation rolls, I think these merits are much more extreme. Whereas before if your fast-talking con man wanted to be useful in combat he had to pick up a gun like everyone else (with the appropriate expenditure of dots and experience if he wanted to be anything like good at it), now he can take a three to five dot merit and with just the attributes he undoubtedly already has be perhaps the most, and definitely one of the most, invaluable members of the party in that sphere.<br /> <br /> That sense of groundedness, of creativity working within certain limits, was always one of the things that greatly defined NWoD for me. While you could make characters with a great degree of flexibility, skills, and interests as opposed to cardboard cutouts, you needed to pick your choices. You could be a superb academic and a good marksmen, but even then that meant you were not going to be a superb academic and a good talker (to use an obviously oversimplified, stripped-down version of character creation), and you probably wouldn't be as good as someone who prioritized marksmanship or physicality. This was important, to me at least, as it reinforced the idea that you were not playing a superhero. Even supernaturals were at base humans, who had many of the limitations and vulnerabilities of your average mortal, as was befitting to a horror game. So the idea that suddenly you can get two for the price of one is something I have issue with both due to the gameplay concerns raised above and from the standpoint of tone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468023#post468023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yes. I did, actually. Because &quot;fiction&quot; does not mean &quot;all fiction&quot;. To me, certain affordances in simplifying the role of technology in stories can be valuable. Emulating Hellraiser 8 is a reasonable fiction choice to me here (I liked Hellraiser 8, don't judge). Emulating Equilibrium isn't really. Not to me.<br /> <br /> I hope that clarifies.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue that I think needs addressing, as while I do understand that there are varying degrees of artistic license and breaks from reality (and appreciate the clarification), it is also a somewhat subjective issue. Several times a very cinematic fictional example has been put forth as emblematic of the idea behind Hurt Locker, only for another one to be called not in keeping with the spirit/too unrealistic. I am not sure what parameters we are using at this point, and am not sure how helpful such examples are given that we all come from different backgrounds both fictional and in real life. Someone might very well say that cinematic hacking has no basis, while there is precedent for dual-wielding, or vice-versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5497-pierrot-le-fou","user":"Pierrot le Fou","date":". 04-04-2015, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5497-pierrot-le-fou","name":"Pierrot le Fou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T07:34:55-07:00","id":468373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pierrot le Fou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468350#post468350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To continue with the above example, another concern is that with merits like it and Know the Territory mental and social characters now are able to &quot;double up&quot;, so to speak: i.e. using their non-physical skills and abilities to become combat powerhouses. This feels more apt for a game like DnD or Exalted (switching out your attack skill, using certain special martial arts) rather than NWoD to me. While there have always been things like Fighting Finesse (though that was with another physical attribute) and supernatural activation rolls, I think these merits are much more extreme. Whereas before if your fast-talking con man wanted to be useful in combat he had to pick up a gun like everyone else (with the appropriate expenditure of dots and experience if he wanted to be anything like good at it), now he can take a three to five dot merit and with just the attributes he undoubtedly already has be perhaps the most, and definitely one of the most, invaluable members of the party in that sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I believe there should be ways for mental and social characters to help in a combat situation that do not involve actual combat, such a planning, dirty tricks, intimidation, etc., so I really like Merits supporting that kind of play. Physical character are also good at certain non-combat tasks, so why should non-physical character be bad at combat?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think &quot;Know the Territory&quot; steps on the toes of actual combat characters, as it actually increases their combat capability, creating situations where it is easier to win. It is not as if the Merit lets you substitute mental for physical skills to let you inflict damage with the Academics skill, enabling the librarian to overshadow physical combat characters. If I were playing a combat focussed character, I would really like to have a party member with this Merit.<br /> <br /> Finally, I understand your concern for balance, but some of these Merits are balanced by that fact that not everyone should logically have them. If one if your characters is a military tactician it is no wonder that he will increase combat survivability. But when a player wants to buy &quot;Know the Territory&quot; for a character without military, policy or other tactical background (gang warfare?) and no other good reasons to get it, I would not allow it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T08:10:35-07:00","id":468427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468373#post468373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. I believe there should be ways for mental and social characters to help in a combat situation that do not involve actual combat, such a planning, dirty tricks, intimidation, etc., so I really like Merits supporting that kind of play. Physical character are also good at certain non-combat tasks, so why should non-physical character be bad at combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one, non-physical characters should be bad at combat if they do not put their points into skills or attributes related to it. This is a horror game, and the mechanics that enforce limitations and sacrifice even during character creation are excellent features to the system. Secondly I feel that intelligence or charisma do tend to have a place everywhere in the hands of a creative player. I support the idea of mechanics to that end (so that unlike many systems non-combat options are more than just left 100% up to the player), but the simple fact is that many of these merits have direct combat utility that, by the investment of a few merit dots, turn a social character into a weapon. Cohesive Unit and Defender both give your team and yourself massive boosts in combat capability that lack a sensible in game source. In a combat scenario the librarian might well outshine the soldier, if only to the mass of dice he adds to an scenario.<br /> <br /> Why not just add in a basic stunting system? Tricks. taunting, misdirection, etc. would already work off of basic skills. The social tank would use a turn to trick someone and gain a bonus while the soldier just gets two turns attacking (for example). It's like aiming, already part of the system, but tied into skills so other types of characters can be useful. At the same time it creates that utility without requiring devoting merit dots. Doing that decreases utility in some ways. Now the ONLY way a social character can be good in combat is by dumping all his merit dots down one tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","user":"Mr. Feral","date":". 04-04-2015, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T08:28:40-07:00","id":468430,"title":"","content":"Well, for what it's worth, when all you can do is roll your chance die in a long ass combat scene and do nothing other than &quot;Uh, I hide.&quot; or &quot;I stay in cover.&quot; It doesn't feel like &quot;Oh, wow, this is so horrifying, awesome!&quot; it's boring as hell. Being able to do something, however indirect, gives those players more to work with than just stuttering uselessly. Maybe they're not shooting the bad guy, but if they're a good leader, they can direct everybody on who to focus on and stuff, that's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I don't need to kill a monster, but if I can do something more than just cower and be useless, that's great. <br /> <br /> This is also why people shouldn't let their combat characters never take any social skills except for Intimidate, unless they're really into the particular concept. Nobody likes feeling useless, and there isn't really an easy way to teamwork an attack.<br /> <br /> Maybe there should be? Iunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T08:31:43-07:00","id":468433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468430#post468430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for what it's worth, when all you can do is roll your chance die in a long ass combat scene and do nothing other than &quot;Uh, I hide.&quot; or &quot;I stay in cover.&quot; It doesn't feel like &quot;Oh, wow, this is so horrifying, awesome!&quot; it's boring as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can confirm this, having last been in a game where another player's sole combat-related ability was Cool Heads Prevail, which never worked when she tried it due to bad luck with the dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T08:39:14-07:00","id":468437,"title":"","content":"I completely agree that a social or mental character having precisely no utility in combat will often leave that player feeling more bored than anything. But their interaction with the combat needs to be dynamic, exciting, and creative. A trickster lobbing insults at his opponents to keep them off balance or a tactician carefully assisting his team would do that. These merits don't. They give flat, static bonuses to the characters that don't feel mechanically connected to their characters and, I feel, are no more exciting than hiding behind a barrier. They need to be a part of the experience for more reasons than because they have one thing written down on their character sheet. That is a limitation, not an expansion of their options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T11:01:34-07:00","id":468518,"title":"","content":"The trick with that is to simply give those character types something to do with their instant action. Ideally a choice between multiple somethings, with that choice mattering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T22:47:17-07:00","id":469888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468023#post468023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really want to do a book about this stuff. I've actually pitched one more than a few times.<br /> <br /> This kind of commentary is pretty close to my heart. I have some material lined up that might exhibit it, or it might fall flat, depending on your opinion.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>last thought on the matter, perhaps rules similar to social maneuvering would be appropriate (though I suspect that wouldn't fit in hurt locker, I wonder about actual 2e core... ) because &quot;doors&quot; for hacking makes sense as well as multiple types of rolls in some cases. 1 roll to write the virus, 1 roll to talk your way into the building, another roll to patch into the network in the server room, and a final roll to upload the virus.<br /> <br /> also, I haven't made it to hellraiser 8 so can't judge.<br /> <br /> I'll end the babbling about realistic hacking, whilst still being movie plot, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T02:28:29-07:00","id":469988,"title":"","content":"David, let me know if you want me to hack Social Maneuvering (pun intended) for this. I love adapting those rules to other purpose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T07:00:34-07:00","id":470104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=469988#post469988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David, let me know if you want me to hack Social Maneuvering (pun intended) for this. I love adapting those rules to other purpose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was asked if REDACTED could use my Social Manoeuvring system to reflect hacking and stuff in REDACTED. <br /> <br /> Let's see if we can find space. Hurt Locker isn't really a good place for expanded computer rules. But who knows. Down the line, we could get something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T10:43:21-07:00","id":470246,"title":"","content":"I was literally just thinking that Social Maneuvering was the perfect way to reflect real world hacking. It even lets you mix in social skills and laying groundwork, installing programs on the target's computers and then using them as separate actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T20:05:35-07:00","id":470689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=468430#post468430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for what it's worth, when all you can do is roll your chance die in a long ass combat scene and do nothing other than &quot;Uh, I hide.&quot; or &quot;I stay in cover.&quot; It doesn't feel like &quot;Oh, wow, this is so horrifying, awesome!&quot; it's boring as hell. Being able to do something, however indirect, gives those players more to work with than just stuttering uselessly. Maybe they're not shooting the bad guy, but if they're a good leader, they can direct everybody on who to focus on and stuff, that's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I don't need to kill a monster, but if I can do something more than just cower and be useless, that's great.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is where I think Avoidance could shine but currently falls flat, it currently mostly is a glorified way to hide, I'd rather it made characters useful in some way, even whilst role playing a pacifist, or someone who is supposed to be not useful in combat, then they can feel useful, their character can be useful, but they are still in character. This is why I suggested changing it's rules towards the idea of their character incidentally, accidentally damaging the bad guy. bad guy swings, clutzy avoidance causes disarm when his weapon gets stuck in something. Increase risk of tramatic failure. Bad guy attacks avoidance is effective ends up converting damage to bad guy, etc, etc. more things like the power that causes Arm wrack, and again I think it should gain in power to the point where you can 'cause damage by doing things like causing your enemy to punch a brick wall or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T01:02:23-07:00","id":471002,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, my player who is a falconry buff is going to be pleased to see that style get introduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=470246#post470246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was literally just thinking that Social Maneuvering was the perfect way to reflect real world hacking. It even lets you mix in social skills and laying groundwork, installing programs on the target's computers and then using them as separate actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had a thread about this (in the more cinematic context of Bleeding Edge as a cyberpunk setting) a while back, but given the Bleeding Edge standard it was more intended to provide a framework for Netrunner-style &quot;VR hacking.&quot; Even outside that scenario, I still like treating access/permissions as &quot;Impression level.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 04-07-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T17:07:14-07:00","id":471842,"title":"","content":"As to the subtopic of &quot;mental and social characters are double roles in combat with Merits&lt;Angst-pose&gt;&quot; - yes, they can, as they can buy Merits by the XP they gathered that characters not interested in those routes would spend on buying other things, making their mental or social specialization even more profound. It's basically this situation - &quot;You have 500$ - you can buy new shoes to running, two science magazines and a nerf gun. Or you just can buy 25 science magazines&quot;.<br /> <br /> Characters are balanced by the virtue they work in the system having the same pools a character creation and earning the same XP based on the same rules. If you take &quot;Know the Territory&quot;, you can't buy the Allies you need or next Social Maneuvering Style - it's as simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T21:38:46-07:00","id":472147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=471842#post471842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the subtopic of &quot;mental and social characters are double roles in combat with Merits&lt;Angst-pose&gt;&quot; - yes, they can, as they can buy Merits by the XP they gathered that characters not interested in those routes would spend on buying other things, making their mental or social specialization even more profound. It's basically this situation - &quot;You have 500$ - you can buy new shoes to running, two science magazines and a nerf gun. Or you just can buy 25 science magazines&quot;.<br /> <br /> Characters are balanced by the virtue they work in the system having the same pools a character creation and earning the same XP based on the same rules. If you take &quot;Know the Territory&quot;, you can't buy the Allies you need or next Social Maneuvering Style - it's as simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A very good point. Taking a few dots of a Style as a social character to gain some character use is easily equivalent to a physical character taking Allies amongst some social group, or Contacts amongst academic ones. Plus, they can Force doors to begin with; the way combat is designed is that even if you lack intimidate, if you win combat against them, you get what you want, so to speak, which in social cases means they do what you want as if you Forced the door some other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T19:30:58-07:00","id":484182,"title":"","content":"A few additional things I discovered:<br /> Zanshin (Iajutusu 1) is a one dot merit that gives +2 to +5 to avoiding ambushes, compared to danger sense which is a flat 2 for 2. Sure the prereqs are a lot stricter but that's still a huge buff. Also, combining it with Defensive Combat (weaponry) allows a character to benefit triply off the one skill.<br /> Trained Bite (Kino Mutai 1) adds quite a bit of damage. It's bashing, true, and you have to initiate a grapple first, but there are easy ways to avoid both drawbacks. Specifically, Clinch Strike to bite on the first round, and any type of supernatural with a lethal bite or just taking the fourth dot of the merit.<br /> Stronger than You (Strength Performance 4) At first I thought this was just a nice alternative to Martial Arts 5, but on closer inspection it seems like it applies to attacks made with weapons as well, making it vastly more powerful. Unarmed a character with this merit can deal a lot of damage, give him a fireaxe and it's a minimum of six lethal on a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T15:17:55-07:00","id":485774,"title":"","content":"Is there a timeline for when all the updated weapon stats will be released? I'm very excited to come through those. I really like how detailed Armory in NWOD got with all the firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5741-seph","name":"Seph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T18:26:49-07:00","id":485888,"title":"","content":"Will there be stats for specialized vehicles in this supplement? Like tanks, jeeps, motorcycles, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:01:15-07:00","id":486273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=485774#post485774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a timeline for when all the updated weapon stats will be released? I'm very excited to come through those. I really like how detailed Armory in NWOD got with all the firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're definitely not going that far with them. I'll drop some stats soon. But, they're a minor section, not a huge focus of the book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=485888#post485888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be stats for specialized vehicles in this supplement? Like tanks, jeeps, motorcycles, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:46:58-07:00","id":489459,"title":"","content":"Drone Control 2<br /> Kill-switch: You need to have a special merit and roll Intelligence + Computer just to press a Kill-switch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:25:20-07:00","id":489638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=440434#post440434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only observation so far is that the Torturer Merit might be better as one dot, rather than two, especially when compared to Vice-Ridden in God-Machine, which has a similar but broader application for the same price. Or maybe Torturer could do a little more, like add a Specialty to Intimidation or something?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, it looks a bit overpriced/under-effective. Given that integrity is all about dealing with mental stress and torturing people feels so good (and not stressful) to someone with Torturer they regain willpower from it, maybe it should make you exempt from breaking points (and integrity/humanity loss) from torturing people?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T19:24:27-07:00","id":490135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=489459#post489459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drone Control 2<br /> Kill-switch: You need to have a special merit and roll Intelligence + Computer just to press a Kill-switch?</div> </div> </div> </div>The merit represents your regular access to the drone with that feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T01:52:48-07:00","id":490345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490135#post490135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The merit represents your regular access to the drone with that feature.</div> </div> </div> </div> So the only way to get a drone that can self destruct is to buy a special merit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T02:18:26-07:00","id":490349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490345#post490345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So the only way to get a drone that can self destruct is to buy a special merit?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nop, you're misreading what he said. The merit represents your REGULAR access to such a drone.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can try and get your hands on each of these military drones... with a proper availability and proper playing out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:34:38-07:00","id":490409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490349#post490349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nop, you're misreading what he said. The merit represents your REGULAR access to such a drone.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not misreading it. I don't see why you need a special merit for <i>regular</i> access to such a drone.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490349#post490349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, you can try and get your hands on each of these military drones... with a proper availability and proper playing out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Why would you need a <i>military</i> drone for this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These maneuvers work independently of the sophistication of the actual device. An RC car with a mounted pistol and a wi-fi receiver works just as well as a state-of-the-art military drone for the purposes of using this Style. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","user":"NineDaysDead","date":". 04-24-2015, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:39:44-07:00","id":490410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490409#post490409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not misreading it. I don't see why you need a special merit for <i>regular</i> access to such a drone.<br /> Why would you need a <i>military</i> drone for this?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because <br /> a) merit talks about weaponised drones... a.k.a military drones<br /> b) only military drones are going to have a self-destruct mechanism in place in the first place. <br /> <br /> You're either getting these drones from the military, or equally hard place to get. Which requires playing out and getting that shit done. (even if it's crafting it yourself with sufficient Crafts/Science/Firearms/Computer rolls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T05:03:46-07:00","id":490415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490410#post490410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because<br /> a) merit talks about weaponised drones... a.k.a military drones</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm no, and I'm not sure how you can think that given that I actually quoted the section where it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>These maneuvers work independently of the sophistication of the actual device. An <b>RC car with a mounted pistol and a wi-fi receiver</b> works just as well as a state-of-the-art military drone for the purposes of using this Style.</i> </div> </div> </div> So no, it covers both military drones and non-military drones\u200b.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:06:31-07:00","id":490498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490415#post490415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Umm no, and I'm not sure how you can think that given that I actually quoted the section where it says:<br /> <br /> So no, it covers both military drones and non-military drones\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I'm probably going to note that it enables clear and reliable access to drone tech, even if it's amateur. If it's a Merit, you don't have to fuss with procurement regularly; it becomes a thing you can access easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:47:25-07:00","id":490710,"title":"","content":"You may as well ask what's the point of the Contacts merit, if you can get contacts in the police of whatever without the merit. It represents a certain investment that protects your contacts to some extent from the storyteller by saying &quot;this is an important part of the character and I don't want to lose this without very damn good reason&quot;. So without that merit, you have no promise of safety for your drone even if you made it yourself. With it, it's just as safe as Bert the Chief of Police, your Ally, and losing it should have just as much weight as Bert being fired under sexual assault allegations, protesting his innocent and found dead the next day in his apartment, an apparent suicide. Losing a merit means you will always have that thing and shit just got real if you lose it. Also you get the xp back, so you can buy a new thing, so a net zero change in capability, as opposed to losing a non-merit drone, in which case you have to manually acquire new capabilities in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:35:51-07:00","id":490755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490498#post490498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FWIW, I'm probably going to note that it enables clear and reliable access to drone tech, even if it's amateur. If it's a Merit, you don't have to fuss with procurement regularly; it becomes a thing you can access easily.</div> </div> </div> </div> That doesn't answer either of the original questions. Why do you need a merit to make a drone self destruct, and why is it so difficult to press the self destruct button as to require a Intelligence + Computer roll?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:37:48-07:00","id":490757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490710#post490710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may as well ask what's the point of the Contacts merit, if you can get contacts in the police of whatever without the merit. It represents a certain investment that protects your contacts to some extent from the storyteller by saying &quot;this is an important part of the character and I don't want to lose this without very damn good reason&quot;. So without that merit, you have no promise of safety for your drone even if you made it yourself. With it, it's just as safe as Bert the Chief of Police, your Ally, and losing it should have just as much weight as Bert being fired under sexual assault allegations, protesting his innocent and found dead the next day in his apartment, an apparent suicide. Losing a merit means you will always have that thing and shit just got real if you lose it. Also you get the xp back, so you can buy a new thing, so a net zero change in capability, as opposed to losing a non-merit drone, in which case you have to manually acquire new capabilities in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div> False equivalence. A merit that gives you an unlimited supply of drones is worth something. My questions had nothing to do with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:26:11-07:00","id":491052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490755#post490755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That doesn't answer either of the original questions. Why do you need a merit to make a drone self destruct, and why is it so difficult to press the self destruct button as to require a Intelligence + Computer roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll look at that note when revising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:46:12-07:00","id":491644,"title":"","content":"Strength Performance <br /> \u2022\u2022 Lifting: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, your character may throw heavier objects than normal. Add your character\u2019s Athletics dots to the maximum Size of objects he may throw, and reduce range penalties for object Size by the same amount. </div> </div> </div>Three questions<br /> <br /> 1: Is this style intended to allow you to throw small cars? If you have:<br /> <br /> Strength 5 <br /> Athletics 5<br /> Area of Expertise: Feats of Strength +2<br /> -1 for throwing<br /> <br /> You can throw up to Size 11 objects? For reference size 10 = 2-seat sports car.<br /> With Dexterity 5:<br /> <br /> You can throw throw the size 11 object 24 yards (Long Range) without penalty.<br /> You can throw throw the size 10, 2-seat sports car, 28 yards (Long Range) without penalty.<br /> <br /> This seems... <i>generous</i> to say the least.<br /> <br /> 2: You can throw larger objects but can't use them as improvised weapons? So you can throw objects with Size = Strength+Athletics+Specialty bonus -1 but you're still limited to objects with Size = Strength?<br /> <br /> 3. Under Vigor, Blood and Smoke says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Objects with Size greater than 5 deal lethal damage to mortals, while those with Size 10 or more deal lethal even to vampires. </div> </div> </div>Does this apply here? I can't imagine being hit with a 2-seat sports car is going to be bashing damage for normal humans, regardless of who is throwing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:45:23-07:00","id":491756,"title":"","content":"Preface: I have not played anything. This is pure educated white room guesses. Without play experience, I can't really be more positive than to say &quot;I see no problem with this&quot;, so assume anything I don't mention raises no red flags. Also, I'm not really inclined to cross-check 13 pages of feedback to determine if my point is brand new or different enough to warrant separate mention. From experience, I'll assume I have something new to contribute with.<br /> <br /> Let's go:<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesive Unit:</b><br /> Dot 2 could use some clarification. My first impulse was players attempting to justify why all group actions are team actions deserving of dice benefit. Since that would make the two-dot version the most potent of the bunch, I'm thinking that's very much not the intent.<br /> Suggestion: Limit to Teamwork actions, or require some pre-planning along the lines of Know the Territory before people get to benefit. Something to differentiate the Team from the Troupe.<br /> <br /> <b>At Any Cost:</b><br /> The idea seems fair enough, but as written it goes too far IMO. Why would a Mental merit about trucking on in the face of pain prevent that foot snagged by a halberd from rendering you prone? Why would you see when blinded? Why are you able to counteract the effects of the environment? How can you escape immobilization? Etc. Is that what the Emotional tag is all about? I couldn't actually find a writeup on the tags.<br /> <br /> <b>Defender:</b><br /> This one is...complicated. I'll attempt to sort my thoughts on it.<br /> 1) It seems easy to abuse by designating other troupe-members as loved ones. Unless the intent is to effectively give you 3 extra Willpower for 3 Experiences in dangerous situations, which compares poorly with Specialties and their benefit. The experienced Storyteller likely dreading party splits, the drawback then becomes negligible. The extra bookkeeping involved with off-the-books Willpower is a concern too.<br /> 2) Even without such abuse, the drawback seems to infringe on the Storyteller and his Story. Unless a loved one outside the Troupe gets killed or kidnapped as part of the narrative, the drawback will derail the actual Story in favor of this side-quest where one character has to hunt down her husband's killer or suffer severe penalties.<br /> 3) It seems to me the risk of loved ones is a heavy enough topic that it benefits from coming as a surprise. So why assume it will happen without the Storyteller spoiling his narrative ahead of time? Why assume he is enough of a dirtbag to just improvise such a thing for the lulz? But without such, can it possibly crop up often enough to warrant buying the merit? In an analogy, where is the Arson Insurance merit? Should come up about as often.<br /> Suggestion: From its fluff text I would personally have reworked it mechanically from the ground up to actually enable protection of others. But going off its proactive/reactive mechanics, all I can think of is to at least limit it to one Troupe member or Storyteller character close to the action, plus all loved ones outside of it. That seems like a good middle ground where you get something for your Experiences, but not too much.<br /> <br /> <b>Know The Territory:</b><br /> Two complaints here:<br /> 1) I can't think of a narrative justification for the Speed increase during advantage 1. At its mechanical extreme, a few minutes of pre-planning will turn average joes into Olympic sprinters simply from knowing the terrain. Even traceurs only remove environmental penalties.<br /> Suggestion: Let it remove terrain penalties instead. The Initiative increase is potent enough as it is.<br /> 2) I can't think of a narrative justification for the bonus only lasting a few turns. If a character knows the lay of the land well enough to reap bonuses as significant as this merit provides, a short-term memory retention of 3-15 seconds seems counter-intuitive.<br /> Suggestion: Either let the bonus persist throughout the Scene, or let the commander &quot;recast&quot; it by barking orders once the time runs out, with its own dice action. In return, force him to only apply each advantage once, without the powerful stacking currently possible. Giving a glass window Durability 6 against gunfire strains credibility in any case.<br /> <br /> <b>Living With Death:</b><br /> Doesn't seem to be worth it when compared to spending a point of Willpower. As I read it, it adds +4 dice max, at a significant drawback. If your character has to be dry of Willpower and beaten within an inch or her life before benefiting, 2-4 Experiences aren't equal to one Willpower worth of dice, especially if it requires Defense sacrifice on top, as potent as that trait has become in GMC. Hell, a case could be made that a measly +2 dice bonus in return for all your GMC Defense is broken to begin with. All-out was barely worth it in 1Ed.<br /> Suggestion: This is the exact sort of narrative occurrence I thought Willpower was there to represent to begin with. Let players invest their Experiences in more of that.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Object:</b><br /> Suggestion: Could use some clarification, as the fluff now implies contextual bonuses, while the mechanics make them omnipresent.<br /> <br /> <b>Master The Mask:</b><br /> I have to imagine using this with Subterfuge and Intimidation would be infinitely more useful than with Empathy and Persuasion. Looking at Subterfuge alone, it seems you are paying 3 Experiences for +2 dice on most rolls -at the risk of feeling Guilty-, as opposed to paying 4 Experiences without drawback normally. But with the other three Skills, the bonus doesn't seem to be worth it. The rare occasion where lying will be better covered by Empathy than Subterfuge can't possibly weigh up for the former now having become a minefield to use.<br /> Suggestion: To be honest, the merit seems superfluous. Lying and social masks are covered by Subterfuge and Composure as it is, and this one just seems to switch things around while making it even harder to determine which social dice pool is appropriate for an action. I'm know I'm not supposed to second what others have said, but this seems like a perfect example of just adding dice to normal stuff without really making things more interesting.<br /> <br /> <b>Dirty Fighter:</b><br /> Firstly, any merit that requires you have an Attribute value of 4 or 5 before benefiting from it should have that as a prerequisite IMO. Joe average could never benefit from this one.<br /> Secondly, the benefit compared to Willpower use spans from 0-13 dice, if my math serves me. During challenging and dramatically interesting one-on-one encounters, where you actually need a boost, the benefit goes from 0 to +2 dice. When it is a boring, result given, many-vs-one curbstomp battle, only then does the benefit kick in for real. This at the Experience cost of an actually useful Fighting Style, one that doesn't carry potent drawbacks. The problem with that should be obvious.<br /> Suggestion: I have rarely seen a merit better suited to impose Tilts on an enemy. Would be a shame to waste it. The mechanics would get more complicated than I'm willing to consider here, but if Willpower has to be the limiter on this merit, the benefit should be something more potent and interesting than mere Defense reduction. Making an All-Out Attack the prerequisite action would be another, possibly better limiter.<br /> As for the drawback, with the WoD being such a dirty, gritty place, it seems overkill for people to be so sensitive to some practical fighting. Hell, how many fighting styles wouldn't qualify under such a scheme? Better to give immunity or resistance to such tricks to familiar characters IMO. If there has to be social consequences for fighting dirty, that can be handled on an individual character basis. I have no trouble envisioning characters in fact applauding your character's pragmatic kill-or-be-killed attitude.<br /> <br /> <b>Fair Fighter:</b><br /> 1) This one could benefit from some clarity on how it interacts with Intent for the combat. The narrative justification for the effect is really thin to begin with, and breaks down if your character is trying to kill the enemy.<br /> Suggestion: In line with its fluff text, it should require a self-defense or non-lethal Intent on your character's part. I would also call for some social actions before or early in the fight, as holding back out of honor merely from watching the opponent's stance and etiquette seems rather unlikely. With fights lasting less than 30 seconds most of the time (10 turns of combat), the fact that the enemy is fighting an inspiringly noble character is the sort of conclusion the system would normally require perception checks for him to even realize, much less act upon.<br /> 2) If indeed an enemy's efforts are hampered by fighting fair, why doesn't your character suffer the same?<br /> Suggestion: Scrap it in favor of the following: If the enemy is swayed, he becomes incapable of performing targeted attacks, non-grappling prone attacks, and lethal brawling attacks. Furthermore, he will pull his blows so that he can't gain exceptional successes on attack rolls. Your character will suffer the same. Adjust cost as needed.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, seems kosher and/or covered by others already.<br /> <br /> <br /> Phew. That's all for today. I may or may not tackle the fighting merits at some later point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Making Star Wars WoD conversion. Gonna be done when it's done. Hopefully not too long now.","edited":{"userid":2217,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","user":"DarthMRN","date":". 04-26-2015, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2217-darthmrn","name":"DarthMRN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:51:43-07:00","id":491759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=490757#post490757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> False equivalence. A merit that gives you an unlimited supply of drones is worth something. My questions had nothing to do with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, specifically the self-destruct part... I guess that represents the ease and knowledge to construct such things without a roll? <br /> <br /> That does strike me as off. I thought your complaints were not understanding why a piece of equipment external to the character got it's own merit at all, not specific to the infinite-RC-cars-of-doom thing. Yeaaaaaah, my bad! I apologize. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T10:53:00-07:00","id":491776,"title":"","content":"Non-Military drones WILL NOT have a self-destruct button in them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Unless we're going for some really high action movies stuff...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T13:06:22-07:00","id":491878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=491776#post491776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Military drones WILL NOT have a self-destruct button in them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Unless we're going for some really high action movies stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div> Well clearly they do, that's the whole point of the Merit. Once again I refer you to the quoted text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>These maneuvers work independently of the sophistication of the actual device</b>. An <b>RC car with a mounted pistol and a wi-fi receiver</b> works just as well as a state-of-the-art military drone for the purposes of using this Style</i> </div> </div> </div>Since you're rolling Intelligence + Computer I assume this is some kind of software wipe. If that's the case, the normal thing to do would be to write a wiping program (rolling at this time), test it, once tested and installed execute it. You wouldn't write a new program for every drone, you could reuse the old one, and executing a simple program shouldn't require a roll.<br /> <br /> If this is actually some kind of explosive device, shouldn't this be a craft roll? And shouldn't the roll be made before launching the drone?<br /> <br /> I'd be happier if the text read:<br /> <br /> Kill-switch (\u2022\u2022): Your character routinely installs self-destruct systems in her drones and can cause them to self-destruct on command, making any attempts to retrieve information off of it impossible to mundane means. This doesn't require a roll. Characters without this Merit can attempt to install such systems with an Intelligence + Computer for software systems or an Intelligence + Crafts roll for physical systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:19:20-07:00","id":493096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=491878#post491878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well clearly they do, that's the whole point of the Merit. Once again I refer you to the quoted text:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since you're rolling Intelligence + Computer I assume this is some kind of software wipe. If that's the case, the normal thing to do would be to write a wiping program (rolling at this time), test it, once tested and installed execute it. You wouldn't write a new program for every drone, you could reuse the old one, and executing a simple program shouldn't require a roll.<br /> <br /> If this is actually some kind of explosive device, shouldn't this be a craft roll? And shouldn't the roll be made before launching the drone?<br /> <br /> I'd be happier if the text read:<br /> <br /> Kill-switch (\u2022\u2022): Your character routinely installs self-destruct systems in her drones and can cause them to self-destruct on command, making any attempts to retrieve information off of it impossible to mundane means. This doesn't require a roll. Characters without this Merit can attempt to install such systems with an Intelligence + Computer for software systems or an Intelligence + Crafts roll for physical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the contention. I think we're getting into dead horse territory here. <br /> <br /> I will be paying close attention when doing notes on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:59:56-07:00","id":493177,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone has brought this up, but...<br /> <br /> Does the Living with Death merit double <i>all</i> bonuses you get on an All-Out Attack, or just the default +2? For example, if I also have the Fated Ferocity merit at two dots, would I get a +2 to my roll for every level of Bashing damage I take, or just the normal +1?<br /> <br /> In other words, does the multiplier apply before or after other merits/supernatural powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T07:40:42-07:00","id":493588,"title":"","content":"Going over the weapons section the only thing I can comment on thus far is that despite reference to Throwing knives, bolas and the like, there are no actual stat blocks for them. I'm assuming that throwing knives use the same stats for knives, but with range?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T08:16:46-07:00","id":493648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=491878#post491878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well clearly they do, that's the whole point of the Merit. Once again I refer you to the quoted text:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since you're rolling Intelligence + Computer I assume this is some kind of software wipe. If that's the case, the normal thing to do would be to write a wiping program (rolling at this time), test it, once tested and installed execute it. You wouldn't write a new program for every drone, you could reuse the old one, and executing a simple program shouldn't require a roll.<br /> <br /> If this is actually some kind of explosive device, shouldn't this be a craft roll? And shouldn't the roll be made before launching the drone?<br /> <br /> I'd be happier if the text read:<br /> <br /> Kill-switch (\u2022\u2022): Your character routinely installs self-destruct systems in her drones and can cause them to self-destruct on command, making any attempts to retrieve information off of it impossible to mundane means. This doesn't require a roll. Characters without this Merit can attempt to install such systems with an Intelligence + Computer for software systems or an Intelligence + Crafts roll for physical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that NineDaysDead's post specifically is beating a dead horse, they provide a really good alternative to cover other situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:48:29-07:00","id":494134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=493648#post493648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe that NineDaysDead's post specifically is beating a dead horse, they provide a really good alternative to cover other situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine. No admonishment. But, I get that this Merit needs some clarity and consideration. I don't want people to spin their wheels pitching suggestions, because ultimately I'm going to note the issues, and let the writer make the best decision. I don't want to overwhelm potential conversation with that one topic. <br /> <br /> This particular Merit is probably going to get a full rewrite if it gets included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T00:08:06-07:00","id":520604,"title":"","content":"Just ran a game where a player used <b>Avoidance</b> and kept asking to house rule to replace the Persuasion requirements with Subterfuge (probably because it was the higher skill for him) but also because it just made a lot more sense for the spirit of the maneuvers. I would suggest that Subterfuge either replace or be a possible alternative for some characters.<br /> <br /> He also tried using the third dot (<b>Whack-a-Mole</b>) and were having trouble thinking of ways this actually looks in combat barring having the enemy punch a wall. So a couple examples would help (though I blame our storyteller and his improv skills), and specifying that it refers specifically refers to brawl and maybe weaponry attacks (and could maybe be a leg wrack or knockdown tilt instead, depending on the method used?) - Unless it's intentionally left open and you meant to allow bullet ricochets, etc. (Which would be kind of cool, actually, but clarity would help). <br /> <br /> He used it specifically after dropping prone behind one of his packmates, so he was being kicked and stomped at, no real room for arm wracks when you're rolling around on the ground.<br /> <br /> Despite all those things, both the Avoidance style and the Dirty Fighting merits were huge hits with the group and enabled some really cool things. Our Irraka used it to hide and use his sneak attack gift against an enemy while they were all ignoring him. Emphasizing the first dots ability to allow for escape or stealth would really upplay one of the coolest things about the merit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:02:24-07:00","id":528720,"title":"","content":"A bit late to the party, but I really like professional therapist and support network.<a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default82ee-3.html?g=posts&amp;m=1618869#post1618869\" target=\"_blank\"> I have wanted rules for this for a long time.</a><br /> Now the only thing missing is GMC Tilts based <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultc96f-2.html?g=posts&amp;m=1668778#post1668778\" target=\"_blank\">rules for bleeding </a>for complete bliss <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 05-26-2015, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T07:36:18-07:00","id":528773,"title":"","content":"There is a Bleeding Tilt in one of the other Hurt Locker draft documents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:32:31-07:00","id":535057,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, I'm currently working on revisions. I know Punch Drunk had a few questions, so I'm revising it thusly: <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Punch Drunk (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Willpower \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022+<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character\u2019s resolve is unwavering, even when suffering wounds, broken limbs and lost blood. She can fight on past the point that her body demands she quit. When she suffers bashing or damage that would remove her last Health box, you may spend a point of Willpower to keep the last box, and instead upgrade damage in her other health boxes. This Merit has no effect on aggravated damage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:39:00-07:00","id":535156,"title":"","content":"That's really neat and I think a good fix to it. I like the design space that occupies. Awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:58:00-07:00","id":535584,"title":"","content":"That definitely looks a lot better, I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T12:03:25-07:00","id":538659,"title":"","content":"Have to say,a lot of interesting,exciting material being developed for this supplement,very pleased with what Isaw overall,but a few things did stand out:<br /> <br /> Chain weapons,alternate version:<br /> -Why is it\u00b4s Feint move (***) not the same as FS: Light weapons Feint (***)?<br /> <br /> As it stands you get to deny the entirety of an opponents defence,even with a single success, and he is open not just to the chain-wielder but anyone attacking him that turn. its an interesting alternative, but is the difference relevant enough to introduce a new mechanic for an existing tactic?<br /> <br /> That said,I love the synergy you managed to create between the first dot and the second of alternate chain weapons:, taking what could of been a &quot;get-and-forget&quot; first dot and expanding it a whole combat tactic that dictates the pace and feel of the fight to make it distinctive from the use of other weapons,and narratively vivid.<br /> <br /> -The standing up Grappling move: Would of preferred it to allow you to reflexively stand-up if not grappled,re-introducing the ability of grapplers to get back to their feet far more effectively when dropped prone. the knock down effect can be inflicted so ubiquitously in GMC, im surprised it hasn't been introduced yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4144-barr2","name":"Barr2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:00:16-07:00","id":682495,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Tuska-Ate?<br /> Most of the different maneuvers and martial art styles I either recognize or are easily researched, I though have no idea the origins of &quot;Tuska-Ate&quot;<br /> <br /> Would someone please clue me in?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:15:50-07:00","id":682601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=682495#post682495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Tuska-Ate?<br /> Most of the different maneuvers and martial art styles I either recognize or are easily researched, I though have no idea the origins of &quot;Tuska-Ate&quot;<br /> <br /> Would someone please clue me in?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Typo. It's &quot;Tsuka-Ate,&quot; a kata in iaido.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:14:44-08:00","id":781834,"title":"","content":"I've had a couple of campaigns that involved giant monsters. Some of them even involved giant-monster vs giant-monster fights, and in a SciFi campaign we almost had a mech vs monster fight like at the end of Aliens. There was also a campaign where I was playing an Embers Dragon and he had to fight a giant squid monster one on one while the other characters ran around trying to complete an unsummoning ritual or find artillery.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to see some expanded rules and a fighting style for &quot;Kaiju battles&quot; or something, 'cause there are a few different ways you can have a giant monster show up and start wrecking everything, and it's really hard to figure out how to run things from there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T14:41:14-08:00","id":781846,"title":"","content":"That's pretty beyond the scope of <i>Hurt Locker</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:21:27-08:00","id":835100,"title":"","content":"What is the point of Berserker Fighting Style? Last time I saw it, it required 3 dots of other Merit (which I find ugh), and it was mostly about actually debuffing yourself. What was the intent behind the style and &quot;desired&quot; playstyle for it? I can't imagine why I would decide to spend 4 merit points to become Insane, which gives +1 to combat rolls, but forbids Willpower spending. It doesn't seem to do...much...other than hurt yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:10:03-08:00","id":835252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=835100#post835100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of Berserker Fighting Style? Last time I saw it, it required 3 dots of other Merit (which I find ugh), and it was mostly about actually debuffing yourself. What was the intent behind the style and &quot;desired&quot; playstyle for it? I can't imagine why I would decide to spend 4 merit points to become Insane, which gives +1 to combat rolls, but forbids Willpower spending. It doesn't seem to do...much...other than hurt yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first dot is kind of a mixed bag, but it seems like the idea is to use it when you're low on Willpower anyway. If you spend your last point of Willpower to activate the Maneuver, there's no downside, since you wouldn't be able to spend Willpower anyway and the Maneuver allows you to act on your base initiative while Insane. The second dot lets you Intimidate an opponent into doing nothing but Dodge, which can be a pretty useful tactic. The third dot lets you inflict Tilts like a boss, which might do a little damage to you, but is a small price to pay to pretty much end most fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:20:47-08:00","id":835262,"title":"","content":"I can see it as a interesting thing to put on enemies (as they have 1-2 willpower points at most) and who usually have numbers advantage (so they can actually shout at people without feeling like a wasted turn) to utilize the 2nd dot, I guess. And the buy-in cost isn't as inconvenient for npcs either.<br /> EDIT<br /> I guess that for more player-interesting version, I would make it so that Insane Berserker still doesn't have access to normal uses of Willpower, but gain special, &quot;Insane&quot; Willpower options at 2nd and 3rd dots.<br /> EDIT2<br /> ...Insane bestows -3 penalty to Social skill rolls. Second dot of Berserker utilizes Intimidation which is a Social Skill, and might be considered thus a Social Roll; does the Insane penalty apply to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 02-22-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:02:51-08:00","id":835351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=835262#post835262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Insane bestows -3 penalty to Social skill rolls. Second dot of Berserker utilizes Intimidation which is a Social Skill, and might be considered thus a Social Roll; does the Insane penalty apply to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. By RAW it looks like that -3 would apply, but I highly doubt it's intended to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:07:32-08:00","id":835357,"title":"","content":"My groupe of Mages is trying to save a team of dream-trapped currently-possesed human soldiers. I'm probably going to playtest the Berserker merit on the soldiers, which might be entertaining because until now, they were relying heavily on non lethal tactics; Iron Stamina 3 + Berserker might make that approach hard, but not impossible. The Yelling might be a fun way to disrupt their spellcasting, I guess. Any things I should watch out or take notice of with this style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:13:50-08:00","id":835362,"title":"","content":"Couldn't say, I haven't used it myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:17:52-08:00","id":840828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=835351#post835351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. By RAW it looks like that -3 would apply, but I highly doubt it's intended to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. That wasn't the intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Will Rotenberry</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer<br /> <b>Armory: Hurt Locker</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5031-bloodywillpower","name":"BloodyWillpower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:21:00-08:00","id":841260,"title":"","content":"I personally love Falconry and K-9 especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T14:10:33-07:00","id":870613,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Two weapons FS merit:<br /> <br /> -the first dot: really? that is the single most underwhelming first dot in all the Fighting styles.its just...bad. I tought we were done past the &quot;get and forget&quot; days.<br /> An obvious choice would be to alleviate the penalties for using the off-hand weapon by one,wich coupled with a skill specialty would put practiced users of the style on par with naturally ambidextrous people. But id settle for +anything+ remotly on par with the other styles.<br /> <br /> the second dot: Seems convoluted. I feel this is where you dont try and re-invent the wheel and go with the first edition &quot;Deflect and thrust&quot; solution:<br /> -trade damage weapon value for increase defense. the end.<br /> <br /> -Boxing: why are we going back to using merits for very specific combat sistems? couldnt you go with more conceptual designations like say &quot;Combative striking&quot;? that\u00b4d cover boxing as it exists now,but also stuff like french savate,modern kickboxing,muay thai striking elements not covered in martial arts, pre-Queensberry rules bare knuckle boxing,wich defenetly fit with the spirit and the mechanics,but are &quot;locked out&quot; by the labelling.<br /> <br /> -systema: its a specific \u00abstyle\u00bb (its authenticty dubious as all hell,but thats another story). we dont need to backpedal into this. find a general category to label it in,reflecting defensive\\moment principles of several combat sistems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4144-barr2","name":"Barr2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T17:40:09-07:00","id":870789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Two weapons FS merit:<br /> <br /> -the first dot: really? that is the single most underwhelming first dot in all the Fighting styles.its just...bad. I tought we were done past the &quot;get and forget&quot; days.<br /> An obvious choice would be to alleviate the penalties for using the off-hand weapon by one,wich coupled with a skill specialty would put practiced users of the style on par with naturally ambidextrous people. But id settle for +anything+ remotly on par with the other styles.<br /> <br /> the second dot: Seems convoluted. I feel this is where you dont try and re-invent the wheel and go with the first edition &quot;Deflect and thrust&quot; solution:<br /> -trade damage weapon value for increase defense. the end.<br /> <br /> -Boxing: why are we going back to using merits for very specific combat sistems? couldnt you go with more conceptual designations like say &quot;Combative striking&quot;? that\u00b4d cover boxing as it exists now,but also stuff like french savate,modern kickboxing,muay thai striking elements not covered in martial arts, pre-Queensberry rules bare knuckle boxing,wich defenetly fit with the spirit and the mechanics,but are &quot;locked out&quot; by the labelling.<br /> <br /> -systema: its a specific \u00abstyle\u00bb (its authenticty dubious as all hell,but thats another story). we dont need to backpedal into this. find a general category to label it in,reflecting defensive\\moment principles of several combat sistems.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The book is in editing now. You're commenting on play testing notes over a year old. These are not even remotely reflective of the final product. <br /> <br /> And please, try to refrain from being insulting when giving feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:13:23-07:00","id":871175,"title":"","content":"Suppose it is sort of late to offer feedback. tough break,then. As for being insulting,do you mean the tone coming across as too abrasive,or any specific thing I said? (because if this is about the Systema thing, thats is as polite as im going to be on the subject.)<br /> <br /> Honestly,the rest of the book is really,really good, FS merits and combat has improved so much in 2.0 and i feel the overall design direction was the way to go,its annoying to see parts of it go against and slide back to the worst 1.0 gave us in the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4144-barr2","user":"Barr2","date":". 04-22-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4144-barr2","name":"Barr2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:42:53-07:00","id":871212,"title":"","content":"That's how designing stuff works. People design fantastic stuff at their first try only in movies and books. Actual designing usually consists of having a good direction and trying 1000 terrible ideas, and then hammering the least worst one into something actually good, and then hitting a wall with your head because it won't work and you have to try something else. You usually don't see the 1000 terrible ideas in the book, but you sometimes can catch glimpse of them in these Open Devs, as they haven't been hammered down or killed yet. Or because the dev is holding a hammer but isn't sure if he should hit it hard or just a little, so instead they ask you for opinion to see it from different angle. <br /> <br /> That's why a lot of homebrew isn't very good (this isn't a specific jab at someone here, it's something I experienced over years in DND communities) - people don't hammer their ideas enough and post them as finished product too soon, instead of hammering them again and again and again and again. That's why a lot of game masters shy away from homebrew stuff, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:19:42-07:00","id":871249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=871175#post871175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose it is sort of late to offer feedback. tough break,then. As for being insulting,do you mean the tone coming across as too abrasive,or any specific thing I said? (because if this is about the Systema thing, thats is as polite as im going to be on the subject.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Some examples of things that are not constructive feedback:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">really? that is the single most underwhelming first dot in all the Fighting styles.its just...bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tought we were done past the &quot;get and forget&quot; days.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But id settle for +anything+ remotly on par with the other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An obvious choice would be to</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this is where you dont try and re-invent the wheel</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the end.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why are we going back to using merits for very specific combat sistems</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its a specific \u00abstyle\u00bb (its authenticty dubious as all hell,but thats another story). we dont need to backpedal into this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some examples of things that could have been constructive feedback if it had come at a more timely manner, and hadn't been buried in a disrespectful post:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Two Weapons FS Merit:<br /> (...)<br /> alleviate the penalties for using the off-hand weapon by one,wich coupled with a skill specialty would put practiced users of the style on par with naturally ambidextrous people.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the second dot: Seems convoluted. (...) go with the first edition &quot;Deflect and thrust&quot; solution:<br /> -trade damage weapon value for increase defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Boxing: (...) couldnt you go with more conceptual designations like say &quot;Combative striking&quot;? that\u00b4d cover boxing as it exists now,but also stuff like french savate,modern kickboxing,muay thai striking elements not covered in martial arts, pre-Queensberry rules bare knuckle boxing,wich defenetly fit with the spirit and the mechanics,but are &quot;locked out&quot; by the labelling.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barr2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=870613#post870613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-systema: (...) find a general category to label it in,reflecting defensive\\moment principles of several combat sistems.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-22-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:49:43-07:00","id":871294,"title":"","content":"Yeah. the tone is quite blunt.certainly more than befits the sensitivities of these forums. will take note to dial it down in the future. to be fair,i didnt attack the people designing these,just the design choices i strongly disagree with.<br /> <br /> I didnt just in sooner,because i honestly hadnt picked up on some of them on a earlier read,or worse...assumed someone else would adress it in editing. again,some of the things feel very much against the grain of what the new direction for combat set out to establish,and i find them problematic if they are to be read as an indication of things to come.<br /> <br /> That\u00b4ll teach me to speak up sooner and keep tabs on the progress of ongoing books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4144-barr2","name":"Barr2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:55:13-07:00","id":871309,"title":"","content":"I think it's less an issue of &quot;the sensitivities of these forums&quot; and more an issue of if you want people to respect your feedback, you should offer it with respect to the creator and work they've done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:56:27-07:00","id":871312,"title":"","content":"Implying &quot;This is crap&quot; with no shortage of elipsis usually tends to come off as insulting to most folks.<br /> <br /> So does apologizing for your audience's &quot;misplaced sensitivity&quot;. But what do I know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:26:57-07:00","id":871907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=871309#post871309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's less an issue of &quot;the sensitivities of these forums&quot; and more an issue of if you want people to respect your feedback, you should offer it with respect to the creator and work they've done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Exactly that. <br /> <br /> And yeah. The thing is, if you want us to share first drafts, you have to get that they're first drafts. Things will change. You're getting material at its rawest. There's literally nothing to be gained from saying something is &quot;just...bad&quot;. I might even agree with your reasons, but that doesn't actually communicate reasons. <br /> <br /> This isn't about &quot;sensitivities&quot; (which calling out is pretty disrespectful as well); it's about reading context. You dug up an ancient conversation to poop on it. There have been fourteen preceding pages, 200+ posts that managed troves of productive conversation (which will influence the final product) without just dismissively insulting rough draft material. <br /> <br /> IN AWESOMER NEWS<br /> <br /> We just sent Hurt Locker over to editing. I just sent art notes over to Mike. I'm actually super excited for the art on this book; I think it has some amazing potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:59:42-07:00","id":871930,"title":"","content":"Can't wait for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:41:23-07:00","id":928502,"title":"","content":"I just want to say, at first I thought Hurt Locker was only going to be a book with a list of guns, and some fluff, but after seeing some of these merits I want to buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 07-08-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:27:29-07:00","id":958238,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker has been sitting in art direction for what seems like a long time now. How long does that sort of thing typically take? Is there a ballpark estimate on when it will come out in PDF form? Any chance we could see more open development before it does?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:31:37-07:00","id":958243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/439267-hurt-locker-notes?p=958238#post958238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hurt Locker has been sitting in art direction for what seems like a long time now. How long does that sort of thing typically take? Is there a ballpark estimate on when it will come out in PDF form? Any chance we could see more open development before it does?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really do any more open development. I've handed it off. The text is done. At this juncture, there's really only room for the errata pass. I THINK it's waiting for a couple of pieces of art? But I'm not 100% sure. That's the last I heard, but I'm not always in the loop about art stuff. All I know is that I haven't been handed a copy to proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A 